0970621220767498,0.01223475206643343,0.0163123719394207,0.009812679141759872,0.02701336331665516,-0.002667293418198824,0.010956570506095886,-0.012277747504413128,0.015969008207321167,-0.010295192711055279,-0.009091476909816265,-0.020012415945529938,-0.019959645345807076,0.022758813574910164,-0.015287249349057674,-0.0024268561974167824,0.005076262634247541,-0.01141554769128561,0.004954881500452757,0.011635100468993187,-0.018170921131968498,Autonomous Tool Selection,"AI agents need to interact with diverse external systems or data sources, but manually specifying which tool to use for every query is inefficient or impossible for complex tasks.","Agentic AI systems, especially those interacting with multiple data sources or external APIs, where the agent needs to perform actions beyond its inherent generative capabilities.","An agent is designed to autonomously select the appropriate tool from a set of available tools based on the given query, task, or current state. This often involves an LLM reasoning about the query and the capabilities of the tools, or a dedicated tool-selection module.","The agent can handle a wider range of queries, dynamically adapt to different information needs, and perform complex tasks by orchestrating tool usage without explicit human intervention for each tool call.","RAG applications with multiple data sources, complex task automation, intelligent assistants, code generation with API calls.",
