937,0.0005338917253538966,0.022991856560111046,0.02182588167488575,0.015589212998747826,0.03075643628835678,0.006857290863990784,0.007412862963974476,-0.0050633754581213,-0.0019678245298564434,0.01087916549295187,-0.004422634840011597,0.00521648395806551,-0.021217254921793938,0.007437899708747864,-0.027361610904335976,-0.009725258685648441,0.0021713636815547943,-0.00018494944379199296,0.010820569470524788,0.018089529126882553,-0.010077868588268757,Teacher-Guided Reinforcement Learning,"Training complex behaviors in Reinforcement Learning from scratch can be slow, unstable, or require extensive exploration, especially for multi-stage or diverse tasks, or when specific sub-skills are needed.","Reinforcement Learning scenarios where an agent needs to learn multiple distinct skills or achieve specific sub-goals efficiently, or where expert demonstrations are available.","Introduce 'teacher' agents, pre-trained policies, or expert demonstrations that guide the main 'student' agent's learning process. Teachers can be trained for specific sub-tasks (e.g., scoring goals, standing up) and their outputs, reward signals, or trajectories are used to shape the student agent's policy, often through imitation learning or by augmenting the reward function.","Accelerates learning, improves stability, and enables the agent to acquire complex behaviors by breaking them down into more manageable, guided sub-tasks, often leading to more robust and human-like performance.","Robotics, game AI, learning complex motor skills, multi-task learning in RL, training agents with specific sub-skills.",
