02271094126626849,0.018547523766756058,0.02215055748820305,0.016954505816102028,0.029875362291932106,-0.000553534715436399,0.01593889482319355,-0.006589040160179138,-0.007366369012743235,0.017895935103297234,-0.01000511646270752,-0.017891503870487213,-0.025277163833379745,0.020740367472171783,-0.017344297841191292,-0.01994680054485798,0.002816100837662816,0.010693362914025784,0.02138109691441059,0.022658945992588997,-0.007609816733747721,Self-Play Reinforcement Learning,"Training agents in competitive or adversarial environments often requires a diverse and progressively challenging set of opponents to achieve robust and high-level performance, which is difficult to generate or acquire externally.","Reinforcement Learning in adversarial, competitive, or cooperative multi-agent environments (e.g., games, robotics competitions, negotiation).","The agent learns by playing against previous versions of itself. As the agent improves, its past versions serve as increasingly challenging opponents, creating a self-improving curriculum. This process allows the agent to explore a vast strategy space and continuously improve its policy without needing external expert data or diverse human opponents.","Enables agents to achieve superhuman performance in complex games and competitive tasks by continuously improving against a progressively stronger opponent pool generated internally, leading to highly robust and adaptive strategies.","Game AI (Go, Chess, StarCraft II, RoboFootball), robotics (competitive tasks), multi-agent systems, strategy learning.",
