310610652,0.023201914504170418,0.026295457035303116,0.0010513769229874015,0.031003771349787712,0.004456575959920883,0.014693599194288254,-0.011307910084724426,0.0019138285424560308,0.007503153756260872,-0.008323312737047672,0.0019421020988374949,-0.017774010077118874,0.02043353021144867,-0.029815156012773514,-0.007469936273992062,0.0017686645733192563,0.006157219409942627,0.008384461514651775,0.024028291925787926,0.00850970670580864,Domain Randomization / Reality Gap Mitigation,Policies trained in simulation often fail to transfer effectively to the real world due to discrepancies between the simulated and real environments (the 'reality gap').,"Simulation-to-Reality (Sim2Real) training for robotics or other physical systems, where the goal is to deploy a simulated agent in a physical environment.","Introduce random variations (perturbations) to the simulation parameters during training. This can include adding noise to sensor readings, varying physical properties (friction, mass), introducing delays, or changing visual textures. By training on a diverse set of simulated environments, the agent learns a more robust policy that is less sensitive to specific simulation parameters and generalizes better to the real world.","Improved transferability of policies from simulation to reality, leading to more robust and effective real-world performance for robotic agents.","Robotics, autonomous driving, any application involving Sim2Real transfer.",
