2189547009766102,0.005517276469618082,0.01790371723473072,-0.0062912688590586185,0.008881902322173119,-0.00855113472789526,0.005028329323977232,-0.0021548967342823744,-0.013605160638689995,-0.018254222348332405,-0.02681458368897438,0.01784539595246315,-0.020199976861476898,-0.0023977558594197035,0.014016183093190193,-0.0024336674250662327,-0.0023212716914713383,0.037884294986724854,-0.017429359257221222,Few-Shot Planning with LLMs,"Existing language-driven agents require a large number of labeled examples (language instructions and gold trajectories) to learn each task, leading to high data cost and hindering the development of versatile agents.","Building versatile embodied agents (e.g., robots) that can follow natural language commands and quickly learn new tasks in visually-perceived environments.","Harnessing the power of Large Language Models (LLMs) to generate high-level plans (sequences of subgoals) for embodied agents using only a small number of paired examples (few-shot setting) and in-context learning, without parameter updates.","Achieves competitive performance with significantly less training data (e.g., less than 0.5% of paired training data) compared to baselines trained with full datasets, enabling versatile and sample-efficient embodied agents.","LLMPlanner, SayCan (implicitly, though ranking-based), other LLM-based planners for embodied agents.",
