389763832,0.010069094598293304,0.020919116213917732,0.008314214646816254,0.021288108080625534,0.008179925382137299,0.013576877303421497,-0.005118715576827526,-0.0023789633996784687,-0.0015682720113545656,-0.009104516357183456,-0.012875563465058804,-0.02474311925470829,0.01799122244119644,-0.021623270586133003,0.002004361478611827,0.01570376381278038,-0.0053000845946371555,-0.0029213817324489355,0.03203355148434639,-0.012638930231332779,LLM as a High-Level Planner,"Generating complex, long-horizon plans for embodied agents from natural language instructions, especially in diverse and partially-observable environments, while maintaining modularity and leveraging commonsense knowledge.","Embodied agents operating in complex, visually-perceived environments that need to execute multi-step tasks based on natural language commands. Hierarchical planning models are often used.","Employing a Large Language Model (LLM) as the high-level planner to generate a sequence of abstract subgoals (e.g., 'Navigation potato', 'Pickup potato') from a natural language instruction. A separate low-level planner then translates each subgoal into primitive actions.",Simplifies the overall planning problem by decoupling high-level strategic reasoning from low-level execution details. The LLM can produce plausible high-level plans and adapt them using its pre-trained commonsense knowledge. Low-level planning becomes conditionally independent of the natural language instruction.,"LLMPlanner, SayCan (though ranking-based), LM-zeroshot planner, other works exploring LLMs for embodied agent planning.",
