323525175452232,-0.005991547368466854,0.021465325728058815,0.01975383050739765,0.00874580442905426,0.021452728658914566,-0.014644330367445946,0.018339375033974648,0.0034156052861362696,0.012362097389996052,0.005824368447065353,-0.010972660034894943,-0.017337700352072716,-0.030574459582567215,0.010844883508980274,-0.023351218551397324,0.005350579973310232,0.016781648620963097,-0.0018629608675837517,0.008821364492177963,0.03254270926117897,-0.016271371394395828,Logit Biases for Output Constraining,"LLMs can generate a wide range of text, but for specific tasks like planning, the output needs to adhere to a predefined set of actions, objects, or other constraints, and sometimes prioritize certain elements.","Using LLMs to generate structured outputs (e.g., sequences of actions and objects) for embodied agents, where the output space is known or can be dynamically determined (e.g., observed objects).","Apply logit biases to the LLM's output tokens. This involves adjusting the probabilities (logits) of specific tokens to either encourage (positive bias) or discourage (negative bias) their generation. For planning, this can constrain the output to allowed actions and objects, or prioritize observed objects.",Improves the quality and adherence of the LLM's generated plans to the task's requirements and environmental realities. It makes the LLM more robust to ambiguous instructions and helps in object disambiguation.,LLMPlanner.,
