,0.00046574894804507494,0.005382695700973272,0.024316173046827316,0.011450002901256084,0.02879437617957592,0.006935224402695894,0.016574809327721596,-0.005948428530246019,0.008295172825455666,-0.002480334136635065,-0.0031382839661091566,-0.013266192749142647,-0.025532817468047142,0.01598227582871914,-0.01400670874863863,-0.000625544402282685,0.016455350443720818,0.0035639191046357155,5.668135418090969e-05,0.027550119906663895,-0.014323631301522255,Ranking-Based LLM Planning,"How to select the most appropriate action or skill for an embodied agent when a predefined set of admissible actions is available, leveraging an LLM's reasoning capabilities.","Embodied agents operating in environments where a comprehensive list of admissible skills (e.g., action-object pairs) can be enumerated upfront. The agent needs to choose the best next step from this list based on a natural language instruction.",Use an LLM to rank the admissible skills based on the natural language instruction and potentially other contextual information. The agent then executes the highest-ranked skill. This approach contrasts with generative planning where the LLM directly outputs a sequence of actions.,"Enables LLMs to guide action selection by evaluating and prioritizing available options, especially useful in environments where skills can be pre-enumerated. It simplifies the action selection process by offloading the ranking to the LLM.",SayCan.,
