24112817645073,-0.003516019321978092,0.020017100498080254,0.018142176792025566,0.01364030409604311,0.017421795055270195,-0.006463785655796528,0.01007116585969925,-0.00462627736851573,-0.0006603850051760674,0.007869142107665539,-0.005798409227281809,-0.009507223963737488,-0.0215018130838871,0.009967274032533169,-0.03279969468712807,-0.0026066910941153765,0.0034748916514217854,0.0002719801268540323,0.018162449821829796,0.02602885663509369,-0.0183506291359663,Online Reinforcement Learning for LLM Finetuning,"Pre-trained Large Language Models (LLMs) lack direct experience with interactive environments, leading to a misalignment between their statistical knowledge and the environment's dynamics. This prevents them from effectively solving tasks requiring functional competence.",An LLM is used as an agent's policy in an interactive environment. The agent collects observations and receives rewards (potentially sparse) from the environment based on its actions.,"Apply online Reinforcement Learning (RL) algorithms, such as Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO), to finetune the LLM. The LLM's parameters are updated based on the collected experiences (observations, actions, rewards, next observations). A value function (e.g., an MLP head) is typically added on top of the LLM to estimate state values for the RL algorithm.","The LLM's policy is functionally grounded in the environment, leading to improved performance, sample efficiency, and generalization on interactive tasks. It allows the LLM to learn from direct intervention and trial-and-error.",Adapting LLMs to specific interactive tasks; improving LLM's ability to learn from experience; aligning LLM behavior with environmental goals and dynamics.,
