012079954,-0.006861793342977762,-0.005897411610931158,0.02838118188083172,0.019257288426160812,0.004768455866724253,0.01959875226020813,0.0011678743176162243,0.01452866941690445,-0.00449122441932559,-0.0036888194736093283,-0.0028466987423598766,-0.007876071147620678,-0.010635415092110634,-0.015418922528624535,0.00854579359292984,-0.029426665976643562,-0.002297632861882448,0.004844245966523886,0.009152879007160664,0.009471725672483444,0.026823531836271286,-0.005190382245928049,Behavioral Cloning for LLM Pre-training/Finetuning,"How to leverage existing expert trajectories or demonstrations to initialize or improve a Large Language Model (LLM) policy for interactive tasks, especially when direct online interaction is costly or difficult initially.","An LLM is intended to act as an agent's policy. A dataset of expert trajectories (observation-action pairs) is available, demonstrating desired behaviors in the environment.",Finetune the LLM using Behavioral Cloning (BC). This involves training the LLM to imitate the actions from the expert trajectories given the corresponding observations. The LLM learns to predict the expert's action for a given state.,"The LLM acquires a baseline policy that mimics expert behavior. While it can achieve reasonable performance, the text suggests it often performs worse than online RL for functional grounding, especially in generalization, due to the lack of direct environmental interaction and causal learning.",Initializing LLM policies with expert knowledge; providing a baseline for comparison with online learning methods; learning from demonstrations.,
