-0.006180230528116226,0.013860316947102547,0.013119574636220932,0.011518499813973904,0.011831937357783318,0.00150540960021317,0.014279925264418125,-0.010342502035200596,-0.006525220349431038,0.0037186250556260347,0.005518130958080292,-0.006844819523394108,-0.02683267928659916,0.007931933738291264,-0.026629183441400528,-0.0018729992443695664,-0.0016431392868980765,0.006215950008481741,0.019785962998867035,0.024673214182257652,-0.0119705181568861,Value Head Integration for LLM-based RL,"Reinforcement Learning algorithms (like PPO) require a value function to estimate the expected return from a given state, in addition to a policy function. How can this value function be efficiently integrated with a Large Language Model (LLM) acting as a policy?","An LLM is being finetuned using online RL, where both a policy and a value function are needed. The LLM processes textual observations and goals.","Add a separate MultiLayer Perceptron (MLP) with a single output (for the value) on top of a suitable layer of the LLM (e.g., the last layer of the first Decoder block for Encoder-Decoder LLMs, or the Decoder block encoding the last token for Decoder-only models). This MLP acts as the value head, taking the LLM's internal representation of the observation and goal as input.","The LLM's internal representations are leveraged for both policy and value estimation, allowing for efficient training of both components within the RL framework. This enables the use of standard actor-critic RL algorithms with LLMs.",Implementing actor-critic RL algorithms with LLMs; leveraging LLM's learned features for value estimation; streamlining the architecture for LLM-based RL agents.,
