524228096,0.015674561262130737,0.0218108631670475,0.007004715967923403,0.017176922410726547,0.000184099335456267,0.015039600431919098,-0.01004950050264597,0.010130228474736214,0.0004590005555655807,-0.006331454496830702,-0.005854867398738861,-0.018216976895928383,0.0049387989565730095,-0.02734292857348919,-0.002954625291749835,0.019826484844088554,0.011004704050719738,0.005057032685726881,0.026208244264125824,-0.014083117246627808,Temporal Symbol Grounding,"Large Language Models (LLMs) may struggle to correctly interpret and act upon temporal relationships (e.g., 'then,' 'after') within natural language instructions, especially when the order of actions in the instruction differs from the required execution order.","An LLM-based agent receives multi-step instructions containing temporal connectors (e.g., 'Pick up object A then go to object B' vs. 'Go to object B after pick up object A'). The agent needs to execute actions in the correct temporal sequence to achieve the goal.","Explicitly train the LLM-based agent using online Reinforcement Learning on tasks that involve these temporal symbols. The environment provides rewards based on successful completion of the multi-step task, reinforcing the correct interpretation of temporal order.","The LLM develops a better functional grounding of temporal symbols, improving its ability to execute multi-step instructions in the correct sequence. However, grounding might be easier when the instruction order matches the execution order ('then') compared to reversed orders ('after').","Improving LLM agents' ability to follow complex, temporally-ordered instructions; enhancing reasoning about action sequences.",
