.00664549320936203,-0.018425630405545235,0.0134710893034935,0.016884561628103256,0.004788220394402742,0.015028323046863079,-0.0027050659991800785,0.016212988644838333,-0.006503266282379627,0.0025371371302753687,0.008522126823663712,-0.0015866418834775686,-0.00816147681325674,-0.029111232608556747,0.01532495766878128,-0.02600768208503723,-0.015089435502886772,0.016484476625919342,0.0037827978376299143,0.006600187160074711,0.018033146858215332,-0.013875016011297703,Robustness to Domain-Specific Vocabulary (Flipped Actions),"How can an LLM-based agent adapt to a domain-specific vocabulary where common words are used with altered or 'flipped' meanings (e.g., 'turn left' means rotate right) without losing its functional grounding?",An LLM-based agent has been functionally grounded with standard action definitions. The environment then introduces a specific domain where the meaning of certain action commands is inverted or redefined.,Continue finetuning the LLM using online Reinforcement Learning in the environment with the domain-specific (flipped) vocabulary. The agent's direct interaction and reward signals will drive the re-grounding of these specific symbols to their new functional meanings.,"While initial performance might be poorer due to the LLM's prior knowledge conflicting with the new definitions, the agent can converge at a similar speed to the non-flipped environment. This indicates that the functional grounding method allows LLMs to adapt to and re-ground domain-specific or altered vocabularies.",Developing LLM agents that can operate in specialized domains with unique terminology or re-defined action semantics; ensuring adaptability to context-specific language use.,
