24608063698,-0.010354779660701752,0.016681499779224396,0.008344372734427452,0.010215419344604015,0.025461532175540924,0.0011310053523629904,0.011473244987428188,-0.003462080145254731,0.008385113440454006,-0.008595052175223827,-0.0040590534918010235,-0.006655283737927675,-0.0324452742934227,0.014916915446519852,-0.02368049882352352,-0.0003063624899368733,0.008059356361627579,-0.005486996844410896,0.0020596138201653957,0.02419465407729149,-0.020340532064437866,External Affordance Function for LLM Planning,"When an LLM acts as a high-level planner, its proposed actions or sub-goals might not be feasible or optimal in the specific environment due to a lack of grounding in low-level physics or affordances.","An LLM generates high-level plans or actions, but it's not directly grounded in the environment's low-level dynamics or object affordances. The environment has specific physical or functional constraints.","Employ an external affordance function (e.g., a learned model or a rule-based system) to evaluate and re-rank the actions proposed by the LLM. This function assesses the physical plausibility or functional appropriateness of the actions within the environment's constraints.","Improves the practicality and success rate of LLM-generated plans by filtering or prioritizing actions based on environmental constraints and object interactions, mitigating the LLM's lack of direct low-level grounding.","Robotics, where LLM plans need to be checked against physical constraints; environments where LLMs lack direct low-level interaction and require external validation of actions.",
