4226051280274987,-0.01068096049129963,0.006984518840909004,0.02137967199087143,0.005378372501581907,0.021281035616993904,-0.0037629359867423773,-0.0001912098960019648,-0.007792158983647823,0.0049222237430512905,-0.005775010213255882,-0.007034542039036751,-0.020718401297926903,-0.01888519525527954,0.006698287557810545,-0.01692955195903778,0.0011582371080294251,-0.0038728811778128147,-0.0029766710940748453,0.011265920475125313,0.028195364400744438,-0.020556358620524406,Function Calling (LLM-Tool Integration),"Large Language Models (LLMs) are powerful for text generation but are inherently limited to their training data and cannot directly interact with external systems, perform real-time calculations, or access dynamic information.","When an LLM-powered application needs to extend its capabilities beyond pure text generation by interacting with external APIs, databases, or executing specific code functions.","The LLM is designed to identify when an external tool or function is required to fulfill a user's request. It then generates a structured call (e.g., JSON object) describing the function to be executed and its arguments. This call is intercepted by the application, the function is executed, and its output is returned to the LLM as additional context for generating the final response.","Enables LLMs to act as intelligent agents, performing actions, retrieving real-time data, and integrating seamlessly with existing software infrastructure, significantly expanding their utility.","Real-time data retrieval (e.g., weather, stock prices), executing code, interacting with databases, sending emails, controlling external devices, complex task automation.",
