492054,0.022333141416311264,0.011032606475055218,0.019264187663793564,-0.019127683714032173,0.00278442888520658,-0.01231963187456131,0.010728752240538597,0.013245242647826672,0.0026886588893830776,-0.019204173237085342,-0.012425391934812069,0.012066250666975975,-0.03353260084986687,-0.0029080193489789963,-0.015377632342278957,-0.0037241028621792793,0.0066723269410431385,0.03470832109451294,-0.014291726984083652,Finetuning (Retriever),"A general-purpose retriever (e.g., a pre-trained embedding model for dense retrieval or a BM25 model) may not be optimally effective at identifying the most relevant documents for a specific domain's queries and document set, leading to suboptimal context for the generator.","In a RAG system where the initial retriever's performance is a bottleneck, and off-the-shelf retrieval models or basic statistical methods do not provide sufficiently relevant results for the specific use case or domain.","Adapt or train the retriever model (e.g., a dense retriever's embedding model or a reranker) on a dataset of domain-specific queries and their corresponding relevant documents. This involves creating positive and negative examples to teach the retriever what constitutes 'relevance' for the particular application.","The retriever becomes more adept at finding highly relevant documents for the specific domain and query types, significantly improving the quality of the context provided to the generative model and thus the overall RAG system's performance.","Improving search relevance for niche technical documentation, legal texts, medical literature, or any domain where general retrieval models struggle with specific terminology or conceptual relationships.",
