66278962045908,0.011990348808467388,0.01940767653286457,0.012395297177135944,0.028619589284062386,-0.006839619483798742,0.009373100474476814,-0.004380323924124241,-0.004325614310801029,0.00019938003970310092,-0.013905842788517475,-0.022724825888872147,-0.02855345420539379,0.016565363854169846,-0.02101500891149044,-0.0059203761629760265,0.01928083598613739,-5.9829017118318006e-05,0.010346692986786366,0.040640588849782944,-0.01290491409599781,Oneshot model querying,"How can the agent generate the steps for a plan efficiently, considering the need for quick responses and cost overhead associated with commercial foundation models.","When users interact with the agent for specific goals, the included foundation model is queried for plan generation.",The agent queries the incorporated foundation model only once to generate a corresponding plan based on user-specified goals and constraints. This allows the agent to devise a multi-step plan and provide a holistic explanation without delving into detailed reasoning steps.,"{'Benefits': 'Efficiency, Cost-efficiency, Simplicity.', 'Drawbacks': 'Oversimplification (for complex tasks), Lack of explainability, Size of the context window (token limits).'}","CoT (Chain-of-Thought) and ZeroshotCoT (Wang et al. 2024b, 2023d) exemplify this pattern by generating a complete reasoning chain in a single query.",
