07300547324121,0.02123982273042202,0.019661888480186462,0.009238815866410732,0.025276102125644684,0.008327318355441093,0.013161209411919117,-0.0019854730926454067,-0.007077948190271854,-0.009176087565720081,-0.020779544487595558,-0.019103068858385086,-0.02140618860721588,0.01556062325835228,-0.026859501376748085,-0.014015542343258858,0.0221604872494936,0.0019357568817213178,0.010383264161646366,0.03453630208969116,-0.013197904452681541,Selfreflection,"A generated plan may be affected by hallucinations of the foundation model. How to review the plan and reasoning steps and incorporate feedback efficiently, addressing reasoning uncertainty, lack of explainability, and efficiency concerns.","Given users' goals and requirements, the agent will generate a plan to decompose the goals into a set of tasks for achieving the goals.","An optimization process where the agent iteratively reviews and refines its own reasoning process and generated content. The agent backtracks to verify intermediate results, adjusts its reasoning, and creates a refined plan. Reflection processes and results can be saved in the agent's memory for continuous learning.","{'Benefits': 'Reasoning certainty, Explainability, Continuous improvement, Efficiency.', 'Drawbacks': ""Reasoning uncertainty (evaluation depends on agent's competence), Overhead (increased complexity and maintenance).""}",Reflexion (Shinn et al. 2023) employs a self-reflection model; a Bidder agent (Chen et al. 2023b) uses self-reflection for replanning; Generative agents (Park et al. 2023) perform reflection to update memory.,
