67152416706,0.004560031928122044,0.012547439895570278,0.019111456349492073,0.02438310906291008,0.03198472037911415,-0.0030497130937874317,0.014490765519440174,-0.00853034108877182,-0.01824292726814747,-0.0016396887367591262,-0.009779255837202072,-0.022582458332180977,-0.01883670873939991,0.0024580673780292273,-0.01419301237910986,-0.01230230089277029,0.011016733013093472,-0.001201118458993733,0.018891938030719757,0.04167664051055908,-0.015114103443920612,Debatebased cooperation,"How to leverage multiple agents to create refined responses while facilitating the evolution of agents, addressing diversity, lack of adaptability, and lack of explainability.",A compound AI system can integrate multiple agents to provide more comprehensive services. The included agents need to collaborate on the same task while having their own perspectives.,"Agents share a question, generate initial responses, and then engage in a debate, propagating their responses to each other for verification and providing instructions for comprehensive responses. This iterative process enhances performance and can continue until consensus or a predefined number of rounds, potentially utilizing shared memory.","{'Benefits': 'Adaptability, Explainability, Critical thinking.', 'Drawbacks': 'Limited capability (agent reasoning, argument, evaluation), Data privacy (need to withhold sensitive info), Overhead (communication, computation), Scalability preservation (complexity with increasing agents).'}",crewAI provides a multi-agent orchestration framework for discussion; Liang et al. (2023) leverage multi-agent debate to address Degeneration-of-Thought; Du et al. (2023) employ multiple agents to discuss user input and converge on consensus; Chen et al. (2023a) explore negotiation in multi-agent systems; Li et al. (2023) propose a framework including peer rank and discussion.,
