137727662920952,0.014366937801241875,0.007094340864568949,0.024646930396556854,0.011307363398373127,0.01283610425889492,-0.009905693121254444,0.005617499817162752,0.002759764902293682,-0.0044755274429917336,-0.018484128639101982,-0.014915993437170982,-0.008403059095144272,-0.029305825009942055,-0.011654933914542198,0.00021897423721384257,0.009391787461936474,0.013713592663407326,0.020024050027132034,-0.008085806854069233,Multimodal guardrails,"How to prevent the foundation model from being influenced by adversarial inputs or generating harmful or undesirable outputs to users and other components, ensuring robustness, safety, and standard alignment.","An agent consists of a foundation model and other components. When users prompt specific goals to the agent, the underlying foundation model is queried for goal achievement.","Applied as an intermediate layer between the foundation model and all other components. It verifies whether inputs meet predefined requirements (e.g., ethical standards, laws) before delivery to the FM, processing risky or sensitive data. It also ensures FM outputs do not include biased or inappropriate information. Capable of processing multimodal data (text, audio, video).","{'Benefits': 'Robustness, Safety, Standard alignment, Adaptability.', 'Drawbacks': 'Overhead (collecting corpus, real-time processing), Lack of explainability (complexity).'}",NeMo guardrails (Rebedea et al. 2023) ensure dialogue coherency and prevent misinformation; Llama guard (Inan et al. 2023) is an LLM-based safeguard model; Guardrails AI provides a hub listing validators for different risks.,
