0.005158762913197279,0.017553476616740227,0.023959828540682793,0.0055797104723751545,0.028110571205615997,0.0028539008926600218,0.006979021243751049,-0.011482524685561657,0.017160240560770035,-0.007791782263666391,0.004403072874993086,-0.02259034663438797,-0.03252393379807472,0.01685359701514244,-0.021015331149101257,0.0035373903810977936,0.007384603377431631,-0.00805090181529522,0.0033158690202981234,0.022116821259260178,-0.003990225959569216,Agent adapter,"The agent needs to deal with different interfaces of diverse tools, while certain interfaces might be incompatible or inefficient to interact for the agent. How can the agent assign tasks to external tools and process the results, ensuring interoperability, adaptability, and reducing development cost.",An agent may leverage external tools to complete certain tasks for expanded capabilities.,"Provides an interface to connect the agent and external tools. It converts agent messages into the required format or content for tools and vice versa. The adapter can retrieve tool manuals or tutorials to acquire available interfaces and learn their usage, then transforms agent outputs based on interface requirements and invokes the service. It also receives execution results from tools for further analysis.","{'Benefits': 'Interoperability, Adaptability, Reduced development cost.', 'Drawbacks': 'Maintenance overhead (adapter itself, historical tool interfaces).'}","AutoGen allows registering tools with usage descriptions; Apple Intelligence supports writing, image generation, and schedule management across apps; Semantic Kernel orchestrates agents and plugins; SWEagent (Yang et al. 2024a) provides agent-computer interfaces for code commands.",
