6837,-0.005914152599871159,0.012239503674209118,0.020175287500023842,0.009313234128057957,0.046607427299022675,-0.001269126427359879,0.013834662735462189,-0.0025299424305558205,0.004325543995946646,0.0020760418847203255,-0.007840503007173538,-0.018539151176810265,-0.033298756927251816,0.027023661881685257,-0.013453612104058266,-0.008856059983372688,0.010291628539562225,-0.015713008120656013,-0.01398159097880125,0.013931618072092533,-0.019484015181660652,Itinerary,"Managing the routing and sequence of destinations for a mobile agent, including handling exceptions and dynamic modifications.","A mobile agent needs to visit multiple destinations, potentially handling network issues or dynamically adjusting its path based on discovered information. There's a need to separate navigation logic from the agent's core behavior for modularity and reuse.","Objectifies agents' itineraries and routing among destinations. An Itinerary object maintains a list of destinations, defines a routing scheme, handles special cases (e.g., destination does not exist), and always knows where to go next. The agent uses this object for navigation, and the Itinerary object is transferred with the agent.",Enhances reuse and simplifies agent design by encapsulating mobility management. Promotes modularity by separating navigation from agent behavior. Facilitates sharing of tours by different agents. Simplifies the implementation of sequential tasks by associating tasks with destinations and tracking execution state.,"Routing among multiple destinations; saving and reusing travel plans; graphically dispatching agents with predefined itineraries; dynamically adding destinations (e.g., from a Yellow Pages service); scheduling meetings or delivering notifications to multiple users' desktops.",
