3390503,0.0060657174326479435,0.015973756089806557,0.017494456842541695,0.036509111523628235,0.0002710955450311303,-0.013903358951210976,-0.013182902708649635,-0.0030208402313292027,0.004799559712409973,0.008040284737944603,-0.02092529460787773,-0.03471210226416588,0.013721594586968422,-0.009646532125771046,-0.008439383469522,0.01143175084143877,0.0019528166158124804,-0.009807941503822803,0.024910777807235718,-0.022360267117619514,Meeting,"Two or more agents, initially at different hosts, need to interact locally at a specific host to overcome limitations of remote communication (e.g., overhead, firewalls, unreliability).","Agents (e.g., commerce agents) need to find each other and interact extensively, but remote interactions are costly, unreliable, or impossible due to network constraints or security policies. Local interaction at a shared 'meeting place' is more efficient.","Provides a way for two or more agents to initiate local interaction at a given host (a 'meeting place'). Agents dispatch themselves independently to this meeting place, register with a MeetingManager object using a unique identifier, and are notified of other agents' arrivals/departures to enable local interaction.","Enables local interaction between agents from different origins, even if their origins are disconnected or behind firewalls. Reduces communication overhead. Simplifies interagent communication (MeetingManager can act as a mediator). Allows agents to interact locally with an unlimited number of agents and can manage shared data.","Commerce agents searching for, buying, and selling goods; agents needing to access local services on a given host; situations where local interaction is more efficient than remote communication.",
