0019314383389428258,0.008147853426635265,0.019512198865413666,0.0151862483471632,0.049163974821567535,0.011729508638381958,0.00790342129766941,-0.012169375084340572,0.005607062019407749,-0.001603039912879467,0.0031155759934335947,-0.020359346643090248,-0.037993524223566055,0.019097372889518738,-0.011063821613788605,-0.012411627918481827,0.012518483214080334,-0.0020802149083465338,-0.0005903624696657062,0.013868529349565506,-0.012843403965234756,Notifier,Agents need to be asynchronously informed about events or changes of interest without constantly polling.,"In a distributed agent system, agents might need to be informed about events (e.g., arrival of another agent, completion of a task, change in data) that occur at a remote location or are managed by another agent. Polling is inefficient or impractical.","An agent (the Notifier) registers other agents (subscribers) that are interested in specific events. When an event occurs, the Notifier informs all registered subscribers. This typically involves sending messages or dispatching a messenger agent.","Enables asynchronous, event-driven communication between agents, reducing the need for constant polling and improving system responsiveness and efficiency.",Notifying agents of new data availability; informing agents about status changes of other agents or resources; alerting agents to the arrival of other agents at a specific location.,
