0171944759786129,0.0069862171076238155,0.023433443158864975,0.004797365050762892,8.730447734706104e-05,-0.014224675484001637,0.009535497054457664,0.0100010447204113,-0.001078330329619348,-0.027120400220155716,-0.00824000034481287,0.0004285052418708801,-0.01485175546258688,-0.007871291600167751,-0.005080633331090212,0.00032166243181563914,0.000222574410145171,0.031050734221935272,-0.006130495574325323,Context-Aware Data Preparation,How to perform data preparation and transformation steps that are appropriate for the specific dataset characteristics and the requirements of the chosen ML algorithms.,"Developing an ML solution where raw data needs to be transformed into a suitable format for model training, and the specific transformations required depend on the properties of the data itself and the assumptions or requirements of the downstream ML algorithms.","Define 'Data Contexts' that describe relevant dataset characteristics (e.g., presence of numerical features, noise levels, data distributions). Link these contexts to specific 'Data Preparation Tasks' or 'Operators' (e.g., data normalization, missing values treatment, dimensionality reduction). A 'Workflow Planner' component can then use these verified contexts to sequence and execute the necessary data preparation steps via a 'Data Preparator'.","Data is prepared optimally for the selected ML algorithms, improving model performance, reliability, and efficiency. It reduces manual trial-and-error in data preprocessing and ensures compatibility between data and algorithms.","In the Loan Approval pattern, 'Data Context C7 states that one should Perform data normalization on numerical features when using kMeans algorithm'. The Task Assignment pattern illustrates 'Dimensionality Reduction' as a data preparation element.",
