9378280490636826,0.025798838585615158,0.01872020959854126,0.02141306921839714,0.003549509448930621,-0.0006262156530283391,-0.02285691723227501,0.013096955604851246,0.009088242426514626,-0.0011165185132995248,-0.007350245490670204,-0.01186483446508646,0.014329545199871063,-0.02916906028985977,-0.020573876798152924,-0.01115094032138586,0.009856021031737328,0.010119052603840828,0.028815243393182755,-0.014979382045567036,Data Context Monitoring,"How to automatically assess and verify the characteristics of a raw dataset to inform and guide subsequent Machine Learning design decisions, such as algorithm selection and data preparation steps.","Before applying ML algorithms or data preparation techniques, it is crucial to understand the inherent properties of the input data (e.g., data types, feature distributions, independence of features, presence of noise or missing values) to ensure appropriate choices are made.","Implement a 'Data Context Monitor' component that automatically parses the raw dataset (obtained from a 'Data Extractor') and analyzes predefined 'Data Context' elements against the actual data's types, feature distributions, and values. This process generates a binary status value (true/false) for each context, indicating whether it holds for the given dataset.","Provides automated, data-driven insights that guide the selection of appropriate algorithms, data preparation steps, and model configurations. This reduces manual data exploration efforts, minimizes potential errors due to mismatched data assumptions, and streamlines the ML development workflow.","Part of the prototype architecture, the 'Data Context Monitor' parses raw datasets and analyzes 'Data Context' elements. Illustrated in the fraud detection implementation where the system 'verifies contexts C4, C5, and C6 from Fig 2'.",
