,0.0067091695964336395,0.009725204668939114,0.01005155872553587,0.02466941624879837,0.0028987969271838665,0.005166865419596434,-0.014852585271000862,0.005406955722719431,0.00859951600432396,0.008746225386857986,-0.01865430735051632,-0.01563982479274273,0.01663529872894287,-0.012113071978092194,-0.01586049422621727,-0.009390869177877903,-0.0060034762136638165,0.028596293181180954,0.0353054441511631,-0.01742498017847538,Metric-Driven Model Evaluation,"How to select and apply appropriate evaluation metrics for Machine Learning models, especially when the choice of metric is influenced by specific business objectives or data characteristics.","After training an ML model, its performance needs to be numerically evaluated and compared against alternatives. The relevance of different metrics (e.g., Accuracy, Precision, Recall) can vary significantly based on the problem's specific requirements (e.g., minimizing false positives vs. false negatives) or data properties.","Identify relevant 'Indicators' (ML metrics) for the problem at hand. Document when to use which metric, potentially linking them to 'Data Contexts' or 'User Contexts' that specify conditions under which a particular metric is most appropriate. The 'Data Miner' component is responsible for reporting on these evaluation metrics.","Ensures that ML models are evaluated using metrics that are most relevant to the business problem and contextual requirements, leading to more meaningful performance assessments and better-informed model selection decisions.","In the Loan Approval pattern, 'Accuracy' and 'Precision' are identified as metrics. 'Data Context C2 states that Precision should be used for evaluation when Users desire a low rate of false-positives'.",
