.004433255642652512,0.004475545138120651,0.015812044963240623,0.0036536226980388165,0.02270207367837429,0.006728010717779398,0.0025153972674161196,-0.026347123086452484,0.01674666441977024,0.0013183270348235965,0.0068360199220478535,-0.009679320268332958,-0.018013648688793182,0.004663173109292984,-0.01746991276741028,-0.0044042691588401794,0.0014728116802871227,-0.00938093289732933,-0.0019492557039484382,0.026472102850675583,-0.010378120467066765,Context-Driven Workflow Generation,"How to dynamically generate and orchestrate a sequence of Machine Learning analysis steps (data preparation, algorithm execution, evaluation) based on verified contextual information and desired quality requirements.","In real-world ML applications, the optimal sequence of data preparation, algorithm selection, and model configuration steps is not static but depends on the specific user needs, data characteristics, and model constraints identified at runtime or design time.","Utilize a 'Context Analyzer' to parse pattern structures and generate a context analysis workflow, systematically discovering alternatives based on which 'User Contexts', 'Data Contexts', and 'Model Contexts' hold true. A 'Workflow Planner' then interprets these verified contexts, along with candidate algorithms and quality requirements (from the 'Quality Evaluator'), to specify the order of actions to be executed by 'Data Preparator' and 'Data Miner' components.","Enables the semi-automated or automated generation of tailored ML workflows, adapting the solution design to the specific context of use. This increases efficiency, reduces manual intervention, and ensures that the ML solution is optimally configured for the given problem and environment.",The 'Context Analyzer' 'generates a context analysis workflow depending on structure of the graph' and the 'Workflow Planner' 'interprets the veried contexts along with candidate algorithms and species the order of actions to be executed'. Figure 6 shows examples of context analysis workflows.,
