908508598804,0.018390364944934845,0.025067776441574097,0.014190442860126495,0.021301407366991043,0.007031516637653112,0.0008841338567435741,-0.02245711348950863,-0.0019550451543182135,0.0034101109486073256,-0.0034945153165608644,-0.02176627330482006,-0.024306949228048325,0.02192291058599949,-0.013795834966003895,-0.006021709647029638,-0.006459810305386782,0.000532688049133867,0.012720828875899315,0.028090965002775192,-0.011731798760592937,User Context Monitoring,"How to systematically gather and verify user-specific preferences, requirements, or operational conditions that influence the selection and configuration of ML solutions.",Designing an ML system where the applicability or optimal configuration of algorithms and data preparation steps depends on explicit input or preferences from the end-users or modelers.,"Implement a 'User Context Monitor' component that actively collects and verifies 'User Contexts'. This typically involves obtaining input from the 'Modeler' or end-users regarding their desires (e.g., simplicity of algorithm, low false-positive rate). The status of these contexts (true/false) then informs the 'Workflow Planner'.","Ensures that the ML solution design is aligned with user expectations and operational constraints, leading to higher user satisfaction and more relevant outcomes. It formalizes the integration of human preferences into the automated ML design process.",The prototype architecture includes a 'User Context Monitor' that 'verifies User Contexts which needs input from the Modeler'. User Context C3 in Loan Approval: 'Users desire simplicity of the algorithm'.,
