65115874260664,0.014129767194390297,0.01864606700837612,0.023314334452152252,0.009808149188756943,-0.005100090987980366,0.002873152494430542,0.008930129930377007,0.014254695735871792,0.009698683395981789,-0.024288306012749672,-0.027150729671120644,0.007540518883615732,-0.024337729439139366,5.424103164841654e-06,-0.000877800805028528,0.0016805862542241812,0.014078092761337757,0.039160728454589844,0.0026008824352174997,Lambda Architecture for ML,"Real-time data processing requires scalability, fault tolerance, predictability, and other qualities. It must be extensible.","ML applications requiring both batch and real-time data processing capabilities, with high demands for data quality and system robustness.","The batch layer keeps producing views at every set batch interval, while the speed layer creates the relevant real-time speed views. The serving layer orchestrates the query by querying both the batch and speed layer and then merges them.","Achieves scalability, fault tolerance, predictability, and extensibility for real-time data processing in ML systems.",Not explicitly detailed beyond the problem and solution.,
