2831570506096,0.015049101784825325,0.01492069847881794,0.014845425263047218,-0.013544143177568913,0.004117489792406559,-0.003958745393902063,0.01859130524098873,0.01259057316929102,0.002574356971308589,-0.021326271817088127,-0.019883716478943825,-0.0018391577759757638,-0.023965556174516678,0.008632797747850418,-0.01233886182308197,0.007116399239748716,0.016676288098096848,0.027795428410172462,-0.010382596403360367,Reranking,"Improving the relevance and order of results from an existing search system, as initial keyword or even embedding-based retrieval might not perfectly capture the query's nuance or optimal document order.","You have an existing search system (e.g., Elastic, keyword-based, or even embedding search) that provides an initial set of top N results, but you want to refine their order for higher accuracy.","Take the top N results from an initial search system and pass them, along with the original query, to a language model (cross-encoder). This model, having access to the full text of both the query and each document, scores their relevance and reorders them. This is typically a second stage in a search pipeline.",Dramatically improved search accuracy and relevance by leveraging the language model's deeper understanding to reorder results. It's a fast way to inject LLM intelligence into existing search systems.,"Enhancing existing search engines, improving the quality of retrieved documents in RAG systems.",
