15070057,0.016075223684310913,0.013802553527057171,0.016197562217712402,-0.004740139469504356,0.003480300772935152,-0.015205479227006435,0.010757124051451683,-0.007845965214073658,-0.009966566227376461,-0.020506910979747772,-0.038137637078762054,0.009036936797201633,-0.01045268401503563,-0.00597353233024478,-0.0008084350265562534,-0.0056899660266935825,0.009524344466626644,0.013283648528158665,-0.02393168769776821,Model Selection for Latency/Cost Optimization,"Different LLMs have varying sizes, computational requirements, and latency characteristics. Using a large, powerful model for every step in a multi-stage AI system can lead to high latency and cost, especially for less critical or initial processing steps.","Building multi-stage AI systems (like RAG or agents) where different components have different performance requirements (e.g., a fast initial step vs. a more accurate final step).","Select and deploy different LLMs (or different sizes/quantizations of the same model) for different stages of the pipeline based on their specific requirements for latency, cost, and accuracy. For latency-sensitive initial steps (like query rewriting), use smaller, faster models. For critical final generation steps, use larger, more capable models.","Optimized system performance, reduced operational costs, and improved user experience by balancing speed and accuracy across the AI pipeline.","Optimizing RAG pipelines, multi-stage agentic workflows, real-time conversational AI.",
