19619,0.024883996695280075,0.019228069111704826,0.0076231989078223705,0.030437687411904335,0.004662864841520786,0.005318757146596909,-0.003029635874554515,0.0035336839500814676,-0.0009063148172572255,-0.00024446274619549513,-0.008563569746911526,-0.026120861992239952,-0.003004280850291252,-0.013503395952284336,-0.0031597961205989122,-0.011881301179528236,0.013609417714178562,0.0146108977496624,0.021159637719392776,-0.013336765579879284,Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) for AI Reliability,"LLMs are probabilistic and can produce incorrect, biased, or unsafe outputs (hallucinations, errors). Over-reliance on autonomous AI in high-risk scenarios can lead to significant problems.","Deploying AI systems, especially LLMs, in critical applications where accuracy, safety, and reliability are paramount, or where human oversight is legally or ethically required.","Design the AI system to incorporate human review and intervention at strategic points. This can involve humans validating AI outputs before deployment, reviewing flagged cases, providing feedback for model improvement, or acting as a final decision-maker for high-stakes actions. Examples include 'recommendations to an expert that can sort of spot the failure modes' or 'safe deployment options' with human oversight.","Increased reliability, safety, and trustworthiness of AI systems by leveraging human judgment to mitigate AI limitations, catch errors, and ensure alignment with desired outcomes.","Content moderation, medical diagnosis support, legal document review, financial fraud detection, critical decision support systems.",
