162,0.01911432482302189,0.019388321787118912,0.016931897029280663,0.04060948267579079,0.0013594185002148151,0.029911069199442863,-0.0057923984713852406,0.0035721813328564167,0.00443438021466136,-0.005364979617297649,-0.019715027883648872,-0.022967113181948662,0.0038392553105950356,-0.028566958382725716,-0.01206263992935419,0.0034874877892434597,-0.0005830543814226985,0.0014159439597278833,0.023704713210463524,-0.013543241657316685,Memory Management,"AI agents need to maintain context, recall past interactions, and access relevant information over time to provide coherent, personalized, and informed responses or actions. Without memory, agents are stateless and cannot learn or adapt effectively.","An AI agent is designed for multi-turn conversations, long-running tasks, or requires access to a persistent knowledge base beyond its immediate input.","Implement mechanisms for storing and retrieving information relevant to the agent's operation. This includes short-term memory (e.g., ConversationBufferMemory for recent conversational turns) and long-term memory (e.g., vector stores for persistent knowledge, often integrated with RAG).","Enables agents to maintain conversational context, personalize interactions, learn from past experiences, and leverage a broader knowledge base, leading to more intelligent and effective agent behavior.","Chatbots maintaining conversation history, agents recalling user preferences, agents accessing enterprise data for informed decisions, self-improving agents.",
