1845,0.007158638443797827,0.02016245760023594,0.004941471852362156,0.017590736970305443,-0.007483342662453651,0.006493859924376011,-0.011025086045265198,0.0236570555716753,0.005804807413369417,-0.003973238170146942,-0.021547751501202583,-0.030675970017910004,0.01655474677681923,-0.01962084323167801,-0.005019279196858406,0.004211615305393934,0.00019332183001097292,0.01648245006799698,0.016864482313394547,-0.009513933211565018,Deterministic Chain (Hardcoded Steps),"How to augment GenAI models with tool calling for well-defined tasks while ensuring predictability, auditability, and minimizing latency by avoiding LLM orchestration decisions.",Well-defined tasks with predictable workflows where consistency and auditing are top priorities. There is no need for on-the-fly decisions by the LLM regarding tool selection or order.,"The developer explicitly defines the sequence of tool or model calls and their parameters. The system follows a predefined, fixed workflow for all requests. An example is a RAG chain (Retrieve, Augment, Generate).","Offers the highest predictability and auditability, typically lower latency due to fewer LLM calls for orchestration, and is easier to test and validate. However, it is inflexible, requires code changes for adaptation, and can become complex to maintain as logic branches grow.","Welldefined tasks, static pipelines such as basic RAG, no need for on-the-fly decisions.",
