6371663883328438,0.0025166510604321957,0.017101788893342018,0.016472227871418,0.021401146426796913,0.00036450487095862627,0.014517164789140224,-0.005131084471940994,0.011124965734779835,0.004314144607633352,-0.008869651705026627,-0.013498272746801376,-0.023247573524713516,0.01620154082775116,-0.015832141041755676,-0.008108852431178093,0.005713825114071369,0.0010931225260719657,0.012570160441100597,0.02159181609749794,-0.012768113985657692,Single-agent System,"How to handle moderate to complex queries within a cohesive domain, allowing for dynamic, context-aware decisions and tool usage, without the overhead of multiple specialized agents.","Varied user queries within a cohesive domain or product area where certain queries or conditions warrant dynamic tool usage (e.g., fetching customer data), and more flexibility than a deterministic chain is required.","An LLM orchestrates a single, coordinated flow of logic. It adaptively decides which tools to use, when to make additional LLM calls, and when to stop. It can reason, iterate through tool/LLM calls, integrate tool outputs, and return a cohesive response.","Provides flexibility, allowing the agent to adapt to new or unexpected queries and loop through repeated calls to refine results. It is simpler to debug than multi-agent setups but less predictable than deterministic chains. Risks include repeated/invalid tool calls and infinite loops if not properly constrained.","Moderate to complex queries in the same domain, some dynamic decisions without the overhead of multiple specialized agents.",
