89931711555,0.006759851239621639,0.023411132395267487,0.015312537550926208,0.039410773664712906,0.004556294996291399,0.016091354191303253,-0.0028513509314507246,0.000332818366587162,0.005783309228718281,-0.008707577362656593,-0.017383376136422157,-0.02216288261115551,0.019648602232336998,-0.013259930536150932,-0.019238192588090897,0.010929711163043976,-0.0070930467918515205,0.011269860900938511,0.0260145366191864,-0.008826478384435177,Multi-agent System,"How to handle large or cross-functional domains, where multiple expert agents with distinct logic, conversation contexts, or large, specialized tool sets are required, or to facilitate advanced collaboration.","Distinct problem areas or skill sets (e.g., coding agent, finance agent), where each agent needs access to domain-specific context or prompts, or when the overall tool set is too large for a single agent's schema. Also used for implementing reflection, critique, or back-and-forth collaboration among agents.","Two or more specialized agents exchange messages or collaborate on tasks. Each agent possesses its own domain expertise, context, and potentially distinct tool sets. A separate coordinator or AI supervisor (either an LLM or a rule-based router) directs requests or manages handoffs between agents.","Offers a highly modular approach that scales to large, complex enterprise workflows and facilitates advanced multistep or multiperspective reasoning. However, it is complex to orchestrate, harder to trace and debug, requires a robust routing strategy, and carries increased risks of infinite loops or tasks bouncing between agents.","Large or cross-functional domains, multiple expert agents with distinct logic or conversation contexts.",
