01392076606862247,0.01883193664252758,0.015630358830094337,0.008358154445886612,0.025027528405189514,-0.008011378347873688,0.0053262487053871155,-0.0019252246711403131,0.01603671908378601,0.009758885018527508,-0.00795873161405325,-0.02410137467086315,-0.020381152629852295,0.0034817922860383987,-0.03411201015114784,-0.001325604971498251,-0.008186230435967445,-0.005105584394186735,0.014949719421565533,0.03289782255887985,-0.012160107493400574,Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG),"How to enable an LLM to generate responses based on up-to-date, specific, or proprietary external knowledge that was not part of its training data, while reducing hallucinations.","Scenarios where LLMs need to answer questions or generate content using information beyond their pre-trained knowledge, often from a specific knowledge base, documents, or real-time data.","A process that involves: 1. Retrieving relevant context (e.g., top-k results from a vector index) based on a user's request. 2. Augmenting the original prompt by combining the user request with the retrieved context. 3. Sending this augmented prompt to an LLM to generate a response.","LLMs can provide more accurate, contextually relevant, and up-to-date answers, grounded in specific data, and with reduced hallucination. It also makes the LLM's knowledge source auditable.","Answering questions from specific documents, chatbots needing access to proprietary information, generating summaries based on provided texts.",
