5,0.004668085370212793,0.01645008847117424,0.01731564663350582,0.020733078941702843,0.0043441480956971645,0.007326269056648016,-0.013377614319324493,0.013790169730782509,0.007553741801530123,-0.006035542115569115,-0.012397276237607002,-0.024464569985866547,0.0137445954605937,-0.01323336735367775,-0.00821666419506073,0.009437448345124722,-0.00573678920045495,0.012687480077147484,0.014147511683404446,-0.022189196199178696,Agent Supervisor / Coordinator,"How to manage and orchestrate multiple specialized agents in a multi-agent system, directing requests to the appropriate agent and handling transitions or collaborations between them.","Multi-agent systems where different agents have distinct problem areas, skill sets, or tool sets, and a central mechanism is needed to route tasks, manage handoffs, and ensure cohesive operation.","Introduce a dedicated 'coordinator' or 'AI supervisor' component. This supervisor (which can be another LLM or a rule-based router) receives initial requests, determines which specialized agent(s) are best suited to handle the task, delegates the request, and manages the flow of information or control between agents.",Enables modularity and scalability in complex domains by allowing specialized agents to focus on their expertise. Simplifies the overall architecture by centralizing routing logic.,"Delegating tasks in a customer assistant system (e.g., to a shopping assistant or customer support agent), orchestrating complex workflows across different functional domains.",
