4221556186676,0.011591295711696148,0.014127041213214397,0.03130115568637848,-0.00584995886310935,0.022167092189192772,0.0015062402235344052,0.0036898571997880936,0.003304173471406102,-0.01426924392580986,-0.012678233906626701,-0.010791657492518425,-0.0008112623472698033,-0.006249332334846258,-0.022491062059998512,-0.004900763276964426,-0.0013785886112600565,0.015532019548118114,0.03303278610110283,0.006734567694365978,Reframing,"A machine learning problem, intuitively framed as one type (e.g., regression), performs poorly or fails to capture important nuances (e.g., probability distribution, bimodal output, uncertainty).","Machine learning problems where the initial framing (e.g., regression vs. classification) limits the model's ability to learn the target effectively or capture desired information (e.g., uncertainty, specific objectives).","Change the representation of the output of a machine learning problem. For example, reframe a regression problem (predicting a continuous value) as a multiclass classification problem (predicting probabilities across discrete bins) or vice versa.","Improves task performance by allowing the model to capture more complex target distributions (e.g., bimodal, skewed), express uncertainty, or align better with specific business objectives (e.g., watch time vs. click-through rate for recommendations).","Predicting rainfall amount (regression to multiclass classification for probability distribution), predicting protein folding structure (distance as classification), recommendation systems (classification to regression of user characteristics), baby weight prediction (regression to multiclass classification).",
