013271723873913288,0.0067580342292785645,0.025995997712016106,0.003235820448026061,0.009453698061406612,-0.0019197403453290462,0.0020468116272240877,0.014538194984197617,0.0005616697599180043,-0.01188221387565136,-0.025414591655135155,0.004323157947510481,-0.029245294630527496,-0.010653031058609486,-0.027846945449709892,-0.008782698772847652,0.020736079663038254,0.039433322846889496,-0.017385970801115036,Distribution Strategy,"Training large, complex neural networks on massive datasets is computationally intensive and time-consuming (weeks), hindering experimentation and increasing costs.","Training deep learning models with millions/billions of parameters on terabytes of data, where single-device training is infeasible or too slow.","Accelerate training by distributing the computational effort across multiple machines or devices. This can be done via data parallelism (workers train on different data subsets, gradients aggregated) or model parallelism (model split across devices).","Drastically reduces training times (from weeks to hours), increases data throughput, and enables the training of models that would otherwise be too large for a single device.","Training ResNet50 on ImageNet, large neural networks with billions of parameters (e.g., Neural Machine Translation).",
