446881771,-0.0012580914190039039,0.026006001979112625,0.017231332138180733,0.01748020388185978,0.01760956645011902,-0.010555519722402096,0.009587600827217102,-0.0017394541064277291,-0.0064005558378994465,0.014903710223734379,0.00458296574652195,-0.015487326309084892,-0.01805385760962963,-0.00309148826636374,-0.014501950703561306,-0.0021301633678376675,-0.009256004355847836,-0.015224747359752655,0.02693350613117218,0.03218616172671318,-0.007518516853451729,Hyperparameter Tuning,"Manually selecting optimal hyperparameters (e.g., learning rate, number of layers, batch size) for machine learning models is time-consuming, expensive, and often suboptimal, especially for complex models and large search spaces.","Any machine learning project where model performance is sensitive to hyperparameter choices, and an efficient, automated method is needed to find the best combination.","Insert the model training loop itself into an outer optimization method (e.g., Bayesian optimization, genetic algorithms) to automatically find the optimal set of model hyperparameters. This involves defining a search space and an objective metric.","Automates the process of finding optimal hyperparameters, leading to better model performance, reduced manual effort, and more efficient use of computational resources compared to manual or grid search.","Optimizing max_depth and n_estimators for Random Forest, number of neurons in neural network layers, learning rate, momentum.",
