09910400211811,0.011555108241736889,0.01401092205196619,0.02241913601756096,0.00734099792316556,-0.007096707355231047,-0.00917869247496128,0.015345484018325806,0.0031131384894251823,-0.0031161862425506115,-0.016593357548117638,-0.020646443590521812,0.017251962795853615,-0.015433034859597683,0.0001629161270102486,-0.002746440004557371,0.004308699630200863,0.010854187421500683,0.038526397198438644,0.010907109826803207,Batch Serving,"Applying ML inference to a large number of instances (millions to billions) asynchronously and cost-effectively, when the online serving endpoint is designed for single, low-latency requests and would be overwhelmed.","Scenarios where predictions are not latency-sensitive but require high-throughput processing of massive datasets (e.g., hourly SKU reordering, daily personalized playlists, applying models to entire databases).","Use distributed data processing infrastructure (e.g., MapReduce, Apache Spark, BigQuery, Apache Beam) to carry out ML inference on a large number of instances all at once, asynchronously.","Provides a cost-effective and scalable way to generate predictions on large volumes of data, leveraging the embarrassingly parallel nature of inference. Can precompute results for later low-latency serving.","Applying sentiment analysis to millions of consumer complaints, recommendation engines (precomputing user-item scores), comment moderation systems.",
