226829230785,0.009343150071799755,0.024144615978002548,0.015038489364087582,-0.0038065891712903976,0.03685043752193451,0.00339977047406137,-0.008169199340045452,-0.0024741783272475004,0.0036265626549720764,0.008857936598360538,-0.017599763348698616,-0.016551997512578964,-0.03577486425638199,-0.0089833103120327,-0.0015617238823324442,-0.02056078612804413,-0.009868242777884007,0.0011662114411592484,0.005527591798454523,0.02885991707444191,-0.011282194405794144,TwoPhase Predictions,"Deploying large, complex ML models on distributed edge devices is challenging due to device constraints (size, memory, processing power, connectivity), leading to tradeoffs in accuracy and latency.","Use cases where ML inference is needed on edge devices (e.g., fitness trackers, smart home devices, factory sensors, remote cameras) but the full complexity/accuracy of a cloud model is also desired.","Split the prediction problem into two phases. A smaller, simpler model is deployed on the edge device for initial, low-latency inference. If needed (e.g., high confidence in a specific category), the input is then sent to a more complex, accurate model deployed in the cloud for a second-phase prediction.","Balances the need for on-device, offline capability with the sophistication and accuracy of cloud-hosted models. Reduces network latency and cost by only invoking the cloud model when necessary.","Smart home devices (wake word detection on-device, complex query in cloud), factory floor anomaly detection (simple detection on-device, complex diagnosis in cloud), endangered species tracking (animal detection on-device, specific species ID in cloud).",
