,-0.00937673170119524,0.0241282619535923,0.016694433987140656,0.013164314441382885,0.02411152422428131,-0.0033215852454304695,0.002983239945024252,-8.062744018388912e-05,0.011093872599303722,0.017674367874860764,-0.005433122627437115,-0.021466633304953575,-0.027475105598568916,0.01597459986805916,-0.004878044128417969,-0.004540324676781893,-0.010174008086323738,0.013302218168973923,0.017997561022639275,0.028496017679572105,-0.01003782544285059,Keyed Predictions,"When submitting large batches of instances for prediction (either online or offline), it's difficult for the client to reliably map the returned predictions back to their corresponding input instances, especially if outputs are unordered or processed in parallel.","Any scenario where multiple instances are sent to an ML model for prediction, and the client needs a robust way to associate each output with its original input, particularly in distributed or asynchronous serving environments.","Have the client supply a unique, client-generated key associated with each input instance. The ML serving system passes this key through and returns it alongside the corresponding prediction.","Simplifies client-side logic for matching predictions to inputs, enables efficient distributed processing (without requiring output ordering), and facilitates asynchronous serving and continuous evaluation by providing identifiable metadata.","Batch prediction jobs (millions of inputs), online serving with batched requests, continuous evaluation (joining ground truth), fairness analysis (embedding customer segments in key).",
