475281,0.001207413850352168,0.024044960737228394,0.008606002666056156,0.001418538624420762,0.02575741894543171,-0.009309329092502594,-0.005476687103509903,0.0007698343833908439,0.003313496708869934,0.011891376227140427,-0.01077703945338726,-0.01204578299075365,-0.027664359658956528,0.0047698733396828175,-0.0023460830561816692,-0.009473099373281002,-0.012712271884083748,0.010076009668409824,0.012217573821544647,0.035530876368284225,0.003866389160975814,Transform,"The transformations applied to raw model inputs to create features during training must be exactly reproduced during serving to avoid training-serving skew, but this is often difficult to manage consistently.","Any machine learning project where raw input data needs preprocessing or feature engineering before being fed into the model, and consistency between training and serving environments is critical.","Explicitly capture and store the transformation logic and any associated artifacts (e.g., scaling constants, vocabularies, embedding coefficients) as part of the model graph or an external artifact. This ensures the same transformations are automatically applied during prediction.","Eliminates training-serving skew, simplifies model deployment by abstracting transformation details from the client, and ensures reproducibility of feature engineering across the ML lifecycle.","Predicting bicycle ride duration (extracting day/hour from timestamp), taxi fare estimation (scaling lat/lon, calculating Euclidean distance), text preprocessing (tokenization, stemming), image resizing/color manipulation.",
