194024086,0.004054149612784386,0.00680371280759573,0.005572570953518152,-0.004358325153589249,0.01591809280216694,-0.006735690403729677,-0.006402609869837761,0.026100607588887215,0.009089586324989796,-0.011459633708000183,-0.029447365552186966,-0.002415393479168415,-0.003087918506935239,-0.0041814204305410385,-0.025051414966583252,0.02032911218702793,0.020011089742183685,0.027779556810855865,0.009962276555597782,Repeatable Splitting,"Randomly splitting data into training, validation, and test sets can lead to information leakage (due to correlated rows) and non-reproducible splits across experiments, making model comparison difficult.","Any machine learning project requiring consistent and unbiased data splits, especially when dealing with correlated data (e.g., time-series, user-specific data) or when comparing different models/experiments.","Identify a column that captures the correlation relationship between rows (e.g., date, user ID). Use a deterministic hashing algorithm (e.g., Farm Fingerprint) on this column, and then use the last few digits of the hash (modulo operation) to assign rows to training, validation, or test sets.","Ensures that correlated rows always fall into the same split, prevents data leakage, and provides lightweight, repeatable, and language-agnostic data splitting for consistent experimentation and evaluation.","Predicting flight delays (splitting by date), predicting airport amenities (splitting by arrival airport), general data sampling.",
