9259601831436,0.004439278971403837,0.010288137011229992,0.0070315394550561905,0.011480848304927349,0.023637956008315086,0.008761529810726643,-0.007580375298857689,0.0022372270468622446,0.022554578259587288,0.007730463054031134,0.00879801157861948,-0.02110457234084606,-0.02263530157506466,0.005844260565936565,-0.013626385480165482,0.0026913094334304333,0.009471902623772621,0.00513841537758708,0.005814811214804649,0.04056048020720482,-0.009506057016551495,Windowed Inference,"Machine learning models require an ongoing sequence of instances (historical context) to run inference, or features need to be computed from aggregates over time windows, making single-instance inference difficult and risking training-serving skew.","Models that inherently rely on temporal context or aggregate features over time windows (e.g., anomaly detection, time-series models, sequence models) in a streaming data environment.","Externalize the model state (e.g., aggregated statistics, historical sequences) and invoke the model from a stateful stream analytics pipeline (e.g., Apache Beam, streaming SQL). The pipeline maintains the necessary historical context and computes windowed features.","Enables real-time inference for models requiring temporal context, avoids training-serving skew by ensuring consistent feature computation between training and serving, and efficiently handles high-throughput data streams.","Anomaly detection (flight delays based on past 2 hours), time-series forecasting, sequence models (translation requiring context), stateful features (average departure delay from an airport).",
