7893496076576412,0.010941065847873688,0.016128096729516983,0.012008225545287132,0.019557032734155655,0.021380780264735222,0.005329033825546503,-0.014171531423926353,0.004934573546051979,-0.0014231790555641055,0.004610540810972452,-0.016873931512236595,-0.024379372596740723,0.015203169547021389,-0.010439989157021046,-0.0018248929409310222,-0.008871099911630154,-0.00808411929756403,0.022476866841316223,0.035160552710294724,-0.00812864676117897,Workflow Pipeline,"Scaling ML workflows, enabling collaboration among multiple teams/individuals, and ensuring reproducibility and reusability of ML steps (data preprocessing, training, deployment) becomes difficult with monolithic scripts or notebooks.","Organizations developing and deploying multiple ML models, requiring automated, robust, and collaborative workflows for the entire ML lifecycle.","Containerize each step in the ML workflow as a separate service. These individual containerized steps are then chained together to form a pipeline (e.g., using TFX, Kubeflow Pipelines, Apache Airflow) that can be run with a single API call.","Guarantees reproducibility across different environments, enables parallel development by different teams, provides centralized logging and monitoring for each step, and facilitates automation (e.g., scheduled runs, event-triggered retraining).","End-to-end ML workflows (data collection, validation, preprocessing, training, deployment), hurricane prediction model.",
