01883493922650814,0.015540573745965958,0.01873409003019333,0.01926291547715664,-0.005129693076014519,0.0029182732105255127,0.0045306496322155,0.009346812032163143,0.012574346736073494,-0.0025727208703756332,-0.013098116032779217,-0.01707191951572895,0.006146749947220087,-0.018723251298069954,-0.009511479176580906,-0.02574755623936653,-0.0012352693593129516,0.016759123653173447,0.041767608374357224,0.0068779755383729935,Feature Store,"Ad hoc feature engineering leads to duplicated effort, inconsistent features between training and serving (training-serving skew), poor data governance, and difficulty sharing/reusing features across projects and teams.","Organizations with multiple ML projects and teams, where features are complex to calculate, derived from various data sources (batch, streaming), and need to be consistently available for both low-latency online inference and high-throughput offline training.","Create a shared, centralized feature store – a repository to store, document, and manage feature datasets. It acts as an interface between feature creation pipelines (e.g., Apache Beam, Spark) and model development/serving, often using different data stores for online (e.g., Redis) and offline (e.g., BigQuery) access.","Decouples feature engineering from model development, ensures consistency between training and serving features, promotes feature reusability and discovery, improves data governance, and accelerates model development.","Taxi ride cost prediction (Euclidean distance feature), customer churn prediction, recommendation systems.",
