9502298832,0.014756035059690475,0.02274372987449169,0.016939440742135048,0.021473577246069908,-0.0021617840975522995,0.004518803209066391,-0.007106388453394175,0.009820816107094288,0.018839692696928978,-0.003491931827738881,-0.017449473962187767,-0.024308357387781143,0.012349187396466732,-0.01540650986135006,-0.015470237471163273,-0.00559707498177886,0.0085794348269701,0.011511064134538174,0.033476874232292175,-0.001993251731619239,Model Versioning,"Updating deployed ML models (e.g., architecture changes, retraining on new data) can break existing client applications that rely on specific model behavior or output formats, and makes performance monitoring/A/B testing difficult.","Production ML systems requiring continuous updates to models while maintaining backward compatibility, enabling A/B testing, and facilitating performance monitoring across different model iterations.",Deploy each changed model as a microservice with a different REST endpoint (or version identifier). This allows multiple versions of a model to be active simultaneously.,"Ensures backward compatibility for existing users, enables fine-grained performance monitoring and analytics across versions, facilitates A/B testing of new models with subsets of users, and decouples model updates from application frontends.","Flight delay prediction (XGBoost vs. TensorFlow versions), book genre prediction (older vs. newer data), adding explainability to a model.",
