2309076786,0.01239252183586359,0.008741876110434532,0.028951827436685562,-0.01808249019086361,0.008581538684666157,0.0018975463462993503,0.015535910613834858,0.00638705026358366,-0.0087279686704278,-0.014409796334803104,-0.03182022646069527,0.005808499176055193,-0.013112569227814674,-0.017816927284002304,-0.01647360622882843,0.011624842882156372,0.02129170298576355,0.027781981974840164,-0.016794001683592796,Heuristic Benchmark,"Explaining the performance of an ML model (e.g., MAE, MAP) to business decision-makers is difficult without context, making it hard for them to understand if the model is 'good' or 'bad.'","Any new machine learning project, especially greenfield tasks without an existing operational baseline, where the model's value needs to be communicated to non-technical stakeholders.","Compare the ML model's performance against a simple, easy-to-understand, and trivial-to-compute heuristic. Examples include constants (mean/median/mode of label), simple rules (linear trend, most popular item), or human expert performance.","Provides intuitive context for model performance, helps business decision-makers understand the value proposition, aids in diagnosing model problems during development, and can inform whether an ML solution is worthwhile.","Bicycle rental duration prediction, Stack Overflow question answer time, accepted answer edit likelihood, country of answer, taxi fare prediction, weekly sales volume, eye disease detection, denial of service attack detection, movie recommendations.",
