6088,0.02893328107893467,0.012376046739518642,0.01619962602853775,0.022661086171865463,-6.257668428588659e-05,0.001613526837900281,0.0011861129896715283,-0.005796864628791809,0.011954929679632187,0.0033750867005437613,-0.017684202641248703,-0.023190215229988098,0.004383670631796122,-0.023742735385894775,-0.00396826071664691,-0.00949737336486578,0.0018079968867823482,0.01543308887630701,0.034691162407398224,-0.005273507442325354,Fairness Lens,"Machine learning models can inadvertently perpetuate or amplify problematic human biases present in training data (e.g., data distribution bias, data representation bias, implicit/proxy bias, experimenter bias), leading to unfair or inequitable predictions for different groups of users.","Any machine learning project, particularly those impacting human lives (e.g., finance, healthcare, hiring, social media), where ensuring equitable and unbiased predictions across diverse demographic groups is critical.","Apply preprocessing techniques (e.g., thorough data analysis with tools like What-If Tool, data augmentation like ablation) to identify and mitigate bias in data before training. Post-processing techniques (e.g., evaluating model performance across data slices, adjusting classification thresholds, using fairness metrics) are used after training to ensure equitable behavior.","Reduces problematic bias in ML models, promotes equitable treatment of different user groups, increases trust, and aligns models with ethical AI principles.","Loan application approval, clothing/accessory identification, sentiment analysis, credit card fraud detection, Google Cloud Vision API (gendered words), Gmail Smart Compose (gendered pronouns).",
