02290213108063,0.017672734335064888,0.01414234098047018,0.023933041840791702,0.0032131285406649113,0.005169520154595375,-0.006200131494551897,0.003125810530036688,0.015340883284807205,-0.016721824184060097,-0.026807311922311783,-0.011470259167253971,0.002755161141976714,-0.022434299811720848,-0.009728877805173397,-0.010318116284906864,-0.002930344082415104,0.01766890659928322,0.026945646852254868,0.002015159698203206,Multitask Learning,"Having to choose between different problem framings (e.g., regression or classification) when both might be beneficial, or when multiple related tasks need to be solved by a single model.","Machine learning problems where multiple related prediction tasks (e.g., classification and regression, or multiple classification tasks) can benefit from shared learning and parameter updates.","Build a single machine learning model with multiple output heads, each optimizing a different loss function for a specific task. This can be achieved through hard parameter sharing (hidden layers shared) or soft parameter sharing (separate networks with encouraged similarity).","Tasks are learned simultaneously, gradient updates from different loss functions inform all outputs, leading to a more generalizable model and potentially better performance than training separate models.","Computer vision (classification + bounding box regression), recommendation systems (predicting user characteristics).",
