162,0.01544666476547718,0.009888746775686741,0.023179247975349426,0.0005457326187752187,0.016192948445677757,0.009355997666716576,0.0001284470345126465,0.012359442189335823,-0.01256814505904913,-0.017885668203234673,-0.023445075377821922,0.001188761554658413,-0.02297917567193508,-0.01047250535339117,-0.013209700584411621,-0.0027534475084394217,0.013329992070794106,0.03653319925069809,-0.019316432997584343,Knowledge Distillation,"Large, complex machine learning models (teachers) may not be fully utilized, but training smaller models (students) with enough capacity to represent the knowledge can be hard.","When a large, high-performing machine learning model exists, but a smaller, more computationally efficient model is desired for deployment, or when training smaller models from scratch is inefficient.","Train the smaller 'student' model on a large amount of data labeled by the larger 'teacher' model's ""soft outputs"" (probabilities or logits), rather than the actual hard labels. This second training step can employ Useful Overfitting.","Transfers the knowledge from the large, complex model to a smaller, more efficient model, reducing computational complexity while maintaining performance. Simplifies the learning problem for the student model.","Deploying smaller, faster models in production, leveraging knowledge from state-of-the-art but resource-intensive models.",
