0.009188895113766193,0.018279697746038437,0.022593416273593903,0.019303083419799805,0.007387447636574507,-0.0009353538043797016,-0.005514353048056364,0.008804506622254848,0.01623515598475933,0.003194438060745597,-0.027133356779813766,-0.027809275314211845,0.01528670359402895,-0.019723348319530487,-0.0047014751471579075,-0.0007361252210102975,0.0006054380792193115,0.019935347139835358,0.03956647962331772,-0.002052991185337305,Lambda Architecture,"Production ML systems need to support both low-latency, on-demand predictions (online serving) and high-throughput, asynchronous predictions on large datasets (batch serving), which have conflicting architectural requirements.","ML applications where some predictions require immediate responses (e.g., real-time fraud detection) and others can be precomputed or processed offline in large volumes (e.g., daily recommendations).","Implement separate systems for online serving (e.g., microservices with Stateless Serving Function) and batch serving (e.g., distributed data processing with Batch Serving). These systems are often compatible, allowing models to be exported/imported between them.","Provides a flexible and scalable production ML system that can handle the full spectrum of latency-throughput tradeoffs for ML predictions, ensuring both real-time responsiveness and efficient large-scale processing.","Recommendation systems, any ML application with mixed real-time and offline prediction needs.",
