1170387,-0.004309040494263172,0.023751715198159218,0.017660293728113174,0.0189868975430727,0.01247806940227747,-0.012468517757952213,0.003252600086852908,-0.008914458565413952,0.015819896012544632,0.02162398025393486,0.0019144295947626233,-0.024475201964378357,-0.023589013144373894,-0.0007398524903692305,-0.028318094089627266,0.0018768603913486004,-0.006300285924226046,-0.004042336717247963,0.013442430645227432,0.027049267664551735,-0.011475702747702599,ParentChild Retriever,"While smaller text pieces yield more meaningful vector representations (better embeddings), providing only these small pieces to the LLM for answer generation might result in missing broader context.",Embeddings represent semantic meaning. Smaller chunks have better embeddings but lack broader context. The goal is to balance embedding quality with contextual breadth.,Documents are split into larger 'parent chunks' and smaller 'child chunks'. Child chunks are embedded. A vector similarity search is executed on child chunk embeddings to find 'k' most similar child chunks. The parent chunks of these found child chunks are then retrieved.,"Provides broader surrounding text (context) to the LLM, leading to better answer generation. It is especially useful when several topics are covered in a chunk, improving embedding quality for search while retaining context for generation.",Improving RAG results by balancing embedding quality (from small chunks) with contextual breadth (from parent chunks) for the LLM.,
