56617142260075,-0.0011888873996213078,0.01711757853627205,0.020698146894574165,0.00842064805328846,0.012971948832273483,-0.0149242477491498,0.01795889250934124,-0.005412225145846605,0.013022517785429955,0.0011629137443378568,-0.0016264795558527112,-0.026008129119873047,-0.02018936350941658,-0.00047670226194895804,-0.03492517024278641,-0.010309107601642609,0.0023868801072239876,0.007229468319565058,0.005317785311490297,0.03488296642899513,-0.018644196912646294,Hierarchical Retriever (Bottom-up),"How to effectively retrieve context from documents that are organized in a hierarchical structure (e.g., sections, subsections, paragraphs), ensuring both specificity and broader context when needed.","Documents are structured as a Lexical Graph with a Hierarchical Structure, where nodes represent chunks at different levels of granularity (e.g., leaf nodes for small chunks, higher-level nodes for larger sections).","Execute an initial retrieval (e.g., vector similarity search) on the leaf nodes (most granular chunks). Based on the retrieved leaf nodes, traverse upwards in the hierarchy to retrieve other chunks higher up in the tree, providing broader context. Optionally, use top-level nodes to determine which subtrees are relevant for retrieval, iteratively narrowing down the set of nodes for the similarity search.","Allows for flexible retrieval that can start with specific details (leaf nodes) and expand to broader context (higher-level nodes), or narrow down search scope based on high-level topics.","Retrieving context from documents with explicit hierarchical organization, such as books, reports, or articles with nested sections, to provide comprehensive context to an LLM.",
