.023348167538642883,0.0071694753132760525,0.019916556775569916,0.012795318849384785,-0.008304273709654808,0.006695894990116358,-0.0005043522105552256,0.01355455256998539,0.004738156683743,0.006863542832434177,-0.02142328768968582,-0.01468322891741991,0.00591213209554553,-0.03347324579954147,0.005442323628813028,-0.003006624523550272,-0.004762460943311453,0.018627744168043137,0.04151574894785881,-0.014589917846024036,Hypothetical Question Retriever,"The vector similarity between a user's question embedding and the text embedding of an appropriate answer or text source might be low, leading to poor retrieval results.",The goal is to increase the similarity between the user question and the available text for better retrieval.,"An LLM is used to generate hypothetical questions that are answered within the chunks. These generated questions are embedded. When a user asks a question, it is embedded, and a vector similarity search is performed on the previously generated hypothetical question embeddings. The chunks related to the most similar hypothetical questions are then retrieved.","Can yield better results in vector similarity search by matching the user's question against semantically similar hypothetical questions, which are often closer to the 'answer' text.","Improving retrieval accuracy when direct question-to-chunk similarity is low, especially for complex or nuanced questions.",
