657402,-0.01861211471259594,0.001973292790353298,0.015366517938673496,0.0010239925468340516,0.038063064217567444,-0.022046461701393127,-0.0014284993521869183,-0.017211372032761574,0.015854230150580406,0.000329359172610566,-0.0019070605048909783,-0.007957566529512405,-0.01810831017792225,-0.00902972836047411,-0.032832689583301544,-0.0030721293296664953,-0.002357321325689554,0.0015900474973022938,0.0017127617029473186,0.04315197467803955,-0.035644758492708206,Text2Cypher,Cypher Templates and Dynamic Cypher Generation are limited by predefined queries or snippets. The goal is maximum flexibility for natural language to structured query translation.,"Retrieving structured data from a Domain Graph. No predefined queries or snippets are available, or the range of possible questions is too broad for templates/snippets.","The LLM is provided with the database schema and a description of the domain (optionally enhanced with data value samples). The LLM directly translates the user question into a Cypher query. The query executes against the database, and the results are provided back to the LLM for answer generation.","Highly flexible, theoretically allowing the LLM to generate any query. However, this pattern isn't 100% reliable, and its reliability can be improved by fine-tuning LLMs, few-shot examples, or query re-generation on failure.",Answering highly diverse and complex natural language questions against a structured knowledge graph without prior query definition.,
