88239384,0.01824033446609974,0.017163820564746857,0.015353331342339516,0.017275813966989517,-0.019254395738244057,-0.009243684820830822,-0.01532819215208292,0.01585133746266365,0.012205190025269985,-0.006284318398684263,-0.030783185735344887,-0.018069777637720108,0.0001363383635180071,-0.02781638689339161,-0.001765277935191989,-0.003027597675099969,-0.005263506434857845,0.001950711477547884,0.030289167538285255,-0.023562954738736153,GraphEnhanced Vector Search,"Basic GraphRAG patterns struggle to find all relevant context, especially when context is spread across many chunks or requires understanding relationships between entities.",Combining Lexical Graphs (unstructured text chunks) and Domain Graphs (structured entities and relationships). The goal is to retrieve richer context than just vector search results.,"An LLM is used to execute entity and relationship extraction on text chunks, and these extracted triples are imported into the graph. The user question is embedded, and a vector similarity search is performed on chunk embeddings to find 'k' similar chunks. A traversal of the Domain Graph, starting at the found chunks, is then executed to retrieve more context (e.g., related entities, their properties, and relationships).","Retrieves more enriched context by leveraging the interaction of entities within the data, providing higher-quality inputs for answer generation. This comes with increased preprocessing effort and cost.","Enhancing RAG by incorporating explicit knowledge graph relationships to provide a richer, more connected context to the LLM.",
