15854000300169,0.01995282806456089,0.018290262669324875,0.014669706113636494,0.01898364908993244,-0.025945264846086502,0.004544446710497141,-0.004985435400158167,0.017551010474562645,0.00970763061195612,0.00043246359564363956,-0.01810673624277115,-0.01638188771903515,-0.003973964601755142,-0.021638711914420128,0.004938509315252304,-0.011378218419849873,0.005845997482538223,0.014754421077668667,0.028559276834130287,-0.007290231995284557,Reranking,"Initial search results (from keyword or dense retrieval) may not be optimally ordered for relevance, and embeddings might not capture all fine-grained contextual information needed for precise ranking.","Improving the precision and relevance of search results, typically as a second stage after an initial retrieval step in RAG or standalone search systems.","Take the top N results from an initial search system (e.g., keyword or dense retrieval). Pass each of these candidate documents along with the original query to a 'cross-encoder' language model. This model, having access to the full text of both the query and the document, scores their relevance. The N results are then reordered based on these new, more accurate relevance scores.","Dramatically improved search accuracy and relevance, often outperforming embeddings alone for fine-grained distinctions, and providing a quick uplift to existing search systems.","Refining search results in RAG, enhancing existing enterprise search systems, improving recommendation engines.",
