3685492556542158,0.011863915249705315,0.013992715626955032,0.010719836689531803,0.024714305996894836,0.006281719077378511,0.00882082711905241,-0.011104891076683998,0.010228188708424568,0.0015828268369659781,-0.004055725410580635,-0.007487973663955927,-0.02488110400736332,0.012372037395834923,-0.019132917746901512,-0.001524226856417954,-0.005901167169213295,-0.000837917672470212,0.009191373363137245,0.03131589666008949,-0.017301466315984726,LLM-backed Agent (Tool Use),"Large Language Models (LLMs) are limited to text generation and cannot directly interact with external systems, perform real-world actions, or access dynamic, real-time information beyond their training data.","Extending the capabilities of LLMs to perform actions, interact with external systems (APIs, databases), and solve problems that require dynamic information or real-world operations.","Design a system where an LLM serves as the central controller. The LLM is provided with access to a set of external 'tools' (e.g., web search, calculators, APIs for Notion, ERP, CRM, Python CLI). Based on the user's prompt, the LLM decides which tool(s) to invoke, generates the necessary parameters, executes the tool, and then processes the tool's output to continue the task or formulate a final response. This can involve multiple, sequential tool calls.","LLMs gain the ability to perform actions, access real-time data, interact with systems of record, and solve a much broader range of problems, moving beyond mere text generation to become intelligent agents.","Automating workflows, intelligent assistants, complex problem-solving, data entry/modification, dynamic information retrieval.",
