0.015022402629256248,0.002813134342432022,0.014687174931168556,0.015723956748843193,0.018187977373600006,-0.004947081673890352,0.00904044695198536,-0.011625697836279869,0.006150898989289999,-0.0055404528975486755,-0.009892266243696213,-0.019675258547067642,-0.03432504087686539,0.009771022945642471,-0.01319887489080429,-0.008749274536967278,-0.0024213124997913837,-0.0013063005171716213,0.01019857358187437,0.027250980958342552,-0.03178146854043007,Smallest Model for Task (Optimization),"Using large, general-purpose LLMs for every step in a complex AI workflow can be computationally expensive, slow (high latency), and inefficient, especially for simpler sub-tasks.","Optimizing performance, cost, and latency in multi-stage AI systems like RAG or agentic workflows, particularly in production environments.","Decompose the overall AI task into smaller sub-tasks. For each sub-task (e.g., query rewriting, embedding generation, reranking, final generation), select and use the smallest, most specialized language model that is capable of performing that specific task effectively, rather than a single massive model.","Reduced latency, lower computational cost, and more efficient resource utilization without sacrificing overall system quality, leading to more scalable and cost-effective deployments.","Any multi-stage AI system, especially RAG and agentic architectures, where different LLMs or models can be used for different steps.",
