014850443229079247,0.005785410758107901,0.009922711178660393,0.021683458238840103,0.020243002101778984,-0.0013243452413007617,0.006286416668444872,-0.013753876090049744,0.012345735915005207,0.00906492117792368,0.0029512536711990833,-0.012567571364343166,-0.022828681394457817,0.013735728338360786,-0.00801983941346407,-0.007013218477368355,-0.012595033273100853,0.00605884799733758,0.01727023348212242,0.02322237566113472,-0.007500705309212208,Evals,"LLM-based systems are non-deterministic, meaning they can provide different outputs for the same inputs. This makes traditional testing insufficient for ensuring they behave as intended and align with desired goals.","When building and enhancing GenAI products, it's crucial to establish a systematic approach for evaluating the effectiveness of a model's responses, similar to testing in traditional software development but adapted for non-deterministic AI systems.","Evaluate the responses of an LLM in the context of a specific task. This involves defining metrics, scoring outputs (e.g., relevance, coherence, factuality), and judging them (e.g., Self-evaluation, LLM as a judge, Human evaluation, or a combination). Evals are integrated into the build pipeline and performed regularly in production.",Ensures that any enhancements (structural or contextual) genuinely improve the model's performance and align with intended goals. It provides a mechanism to track performance over time and make informed decisions about model updates.,[],
