20415127277374268,0.0297112874686718,0.014670968055725098,0.01860969513654709,-0.014894071035087109,0.00340447248890996,-0.00211318745277822,0.015041176229715347,0.005470117554068565,0.005045185796916485,-0.02753560058772564,-0.026203658431768417,-0.0011661025928333402,-0.02907213196158409,-0.0006772810011170805,-0.002487652003765106,0.005764476489275694,0.010374657809734344,0.03133653476834297,-0.009023556485772133,Hybrid Retriever,"Relying solely on document chunk embeddings in a vector store for retrieval can be inefficient and may lose semantic detail, especially when compressing multiple paragraphs into a single dense vector. This can lead to less effective retrieval for complex queries.","In RAG systems, when the initial retrieval based purely on vector search of embeddings does not consistently yield the most relevant or comprehensive set of documents, or when a faster, less compute-intensive initial search is desired.","Combine searches using embeddings (vector search) with other search techniques, such as traditional keyword searches (e.g., TFIDF, BM25). This involves preparing data for both types of searches (e.g., text index for keywords, vector index for embeddings) and then combining their results.","Yields a better and more comprehensive set of candidate document fragments for the LLM by leveraging the strengths of different search methodologies. It can improve retrieval efficiency and accuracy, especially for diverse datasets.",[],
