082512,0.02344132587313652,0.017745235934853554,0.009969862177968025,-0.010474659502506256,-0.0024036653339862823,-0.01628924533724785,0.01174310315400362,3.0077276278461795e-06,0.00457329535856843,-0.01675586961209774,-0.013981047086417675,0.0009224321693181992,-0.025494370609521866,-0.0015283040702342987,-0.0057701533660292625,-0.0010552586754783988,0.0137626389041543,0.02605053037405014,-0.004531431943178177,Reranker,"Retrievers, especially those optimized for speed or combining multiple search techniques (like Hybrid Retriever), can return an overly large set of candidate document fragments of varying quality. Sending all these to the LLM can bloat the prompt, confuse the LLM, and reduce the quality of its response.","In RAG systems, after a retriever has identified a set of potentially relevant document fragments, but before these fragments are passed to the LLM as context.","Rank the set of retrieved document fragments according to their usefulness and relevance to the original query, and then send only the best-ranked fragments to the LLM. This typically involves using a deep neural net model (e.g., a cross-encoder like bgereranker-large) that can accurately assess the query-document relevance.","Enhances the accuracy and relevance of the LLM's answers by providing a more focused, higher-quality, and concise context. It prevents prompt bloat and confusion, leading to better LLM performance. It can also incorporate user-specific preferences into the ranking.",[],
