5106525961309671,-0.0019644498825073242,0.01587960682809353,0.02489093318581581,0.0001303155586356297,0.018268806859850883,-0.010257015936076641,0.008380287326872349,-0.012475508265197277,0.007509566843509674,0.006198192946612835,-0.0013017456512898207,-0.018148766830563545,-0.015321092680096626,0.002351220231503248,-0.029616739600896835,-0.010058312676846981,-0.002581165172159672,-0.006965124048292637,0.013478431850671768,0.03448646515607834,-0.017061440274119377,Fine Tuning,"Foundation LLMs are general-purpose and may not possess the specific knowledge, style, or nuanced understanding required for a particular domain or task. RAG might provide context but cannot fundamentally alter the model's underlying 'style' or broader domain expertise.","When prompt tweaking and Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) are insufficient to achieve satisfactory performance metrics, and a deeper, more intrinsic adaptation of the LLM's knowledge base or operational style is required for a specific domain.","Carry out additional training to a pretrained LLM on a carefully selected, domain-specific dataset. This process refines the model's parameters to enhance its knowledge and behavior for the task at hand. Approaches include full finetuning, selective layer finetuning, and Parameter-Efficient Fine Tuning (PEFT) like LoRA.","Enables the LLM to become highly knowledgeable about a specific domain or operate in a particular style, beyond what can be achieved through in-context learning. It leads to a deeper realignment of the model's internal workings for specialized tasks.",[],
