00716078607365489,0.015376739203929901,-0.001792804105207324,0.014371390454471111,-0.002708537271246314,-0.007785917725414038,-0.018944095820188522,0.007605527061969042,0.014403426088392735,-0.007558619137853384,-0.02304164320230484,-0.00999270286411047,0.011218825355172157,-0.019888419657945633,0.0021182396449148655,-0.005976297426968813,0.004436148796230555,0.009670916944742203,0.022901209071278572,-0.020572252571582794,Create Docker containers in SageMaker for model training in Step Functions,"Packaging custom machine learning code and its dependencies into reproducible and portable environments for model training, especially when orchestrating complex, multi-step ML workflows.","Data scientists often use custom libraries, frameworks, or specific environments for their ML models. To ensure consistent training across different stages or environments, these need to be containerized. AWS Step Functions can then orchestrate these containerized training jobs.","The pattern describes how to create Docker containers suitable for Amazon SageMaker training jobs, encapsulating custom ML code and dependencies, and then integrate these containers into AWS Step Functions workflows for orchestrated and reproducible model training.","Reproducible, scalable, and portable model training environments, allowing for complex ML pipelines to be built, managed, and executed reliably using Step Functions, improving consistency and efficiency.","Custom ML model training, reproducible ML experiments, complex ML pipeline orchestration, dependency management for ML models.",
