677790760993958,0.015028057619929314,0.00920373760163784,0.011407202109694481,0.0022304721642285585,-0.008314868435263634,-0.022121330723166466,0.015226352959871292,0.003598168259486556,-0.0008577454136684537,-0.018922876566648483,-0.020565541461110115,0.024739999324083328,-0.011984984390437603,-0.0019105083774775267,0.005401527509093285,0.003302218858152628,0.012399782426655293,0.030743451789021492,-0.016894446685910225,Deploy multiple pipeline model objects in a single SageMaker endpoint,"Inefficiently deploying and managing multiple machine learning models, potentially chained together, under separate inference endpoints, leading to increased operational overhead and complexity.","In complex ML applications, multiple models might be involved in a sequence (e.g., preprocessing, main prediction, post-processing). Deploying each as a separate endpoint can be resource-intensive and complicate API management.","The pattern describes how to package and deploy multiple models as a SageMaker Model Pipeline, allowing them to be invoked sequentially through a single inference endpoint, optimizing resource utilization and simplifying API integration.","Reduced operational overhead, optimized resource usage, and simplified API integration for multi-model inference scenarios, leading to more efficient and scalable ML model serving.","Chained ML models, multi-stage inference pipelines, A/B testing of model components, complex model serving architectures.",
