07388654351234,0.017929837107658386,0.0068311369977891445,0.02474331669509411,-0.0074398452416062355,-0.0033956444822251797,-0.0021761623211205006,0.0181952603161335,0.025520630180835724,0.011546389199793339,-0.0032069350127130747,-0.011659035459160805,0.016965173184871674,-0.02933313138782978,-0.0038646631874144077,-0.004941053222864866,-0.0047755460254848,0.007812629453837872,0.027278175577521324,-0.021493205800652504,Perform ML analytics using Amazon Redshift ML,Integrating machine learning capabilities directly into a data warehouse environment to enable data analysts and SQL users to build and deploy ML models without extensive ML expertise or data movement.,Data analysts often work with data in data warehouses (like Amazon Redshift) and want to leverage ML for predictive analytics without moving data to separate ML platforms or learning complex ML frameworks.,"The pattern utilizes Amazon Redshift ML, which allows users to create, train, and deploy ML models using familiar SQL commands directly within Redshift, leveraging Amazon SageMaker behind the scenes for the heavy lifting.","Democratized ML capabilities for data analysts, enabling them to perform predictive analytics directly on their data warehouse data using familiar SQL, accelerating insights and decision-making.","Predictive analytics in data warehouses, SQL-based ML, business intelligence with ML, customer segmentation, churn prediction.",
