5815333426,0.002467441139742732,0.023608189076185226,-0.002768260892480612,0.0028850685339421034,-0.0037904377095401287,0.0016289787599816918,-0.012220922857522964,0.0136049073189497,-0.0062369476072490215,0.0025379550643265247,-0.005788465030491352,-0.01306470949202776,0.02997414395213127,-0.03457694128155708,-0.008297504857182503,-0.016671644523739815,0.015261255204677582,0.01412554644048214,0.03206359222531319,-0.00188138906378299,Cross-Account SageMaker Studio CodeCommit Integration,How to securely access and manage source code for ML projects stored in a CodeCommit repository in one AWS account from a SageMaker Studio Classic environment in a different AWS account.,"A multi-account AWS environment where ML development (SageMaker Studio Classic) and source code management (CodeCommit) are segregated into different accounts for security, governance, or organizational reasons.",Create an IAM policy and role in Account A (CodeCommit) with permissions to access the repository. Create an IAM inline policy in Account B (SageMaker Studio) allowing the SageMaker execution role to assume the role in Account A. Use a shell script within SageMaker Studio Classic to perform Git operations by assuming the cross-account role.,"ML developers in SageMaker Studio Classic can securely clone and interact with CodeCommit repositories located in another AWS account, enabling collaborative and secure ML development workflows across organizational boundaries.",Securely managing ML project code across different AWS accounts; enabling centralized code repositories while maintaining decentralized ML development environments.,
