7242923527956,-0.0016677383100613952,0.006374042946845293,-0.004560411907732487,-0.0015059990109875798,-0.01209667045623064,0.007300485856831074,0.014666383154690266,-0.008686566725373268,-0.021750567480921745,-0.006015046499669552,0.013809059746563435,-0.021407919004559517,0.002005700021982193,-0.002034264151006937,0.004251793026924133,0.00959098432213068,0.021455682814121246,-0.019259445369243622,Custom Containerized ML Training with Step Functions,"How to train ML models on Amazon SageMaker using custom environments, libraries, or frameworks that are not natively supported by SageMaker's built-in algorithms, and orchestrate this training as part of a larger workflow.","ML projects requiring specialized software configurations, specific versions of libraries, or proprietary code for model training, where the training process needs to be automated and managed as a stateful workflow.","Build a custom Docker container image containing the required ML environment and push it to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR). Then, use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate SageMaker training jobs that utilize this custom container image.","Flexible and reproducible ML model training with custom environments, integrated into an automated, fault-tolerant workflow managed by AWS Step Functions, allowing for complex multi-step ML pipelines.",Training models with unique dependencies; integrating custom ML frameworks; building complex multi-step ML pipelines.,
