811716139317,0.010864323005080223,-0.004745445679873228,0.004969604313373566,0.005000761244446039,-0.00945858284831047,-0.012591725215315819,0.01529860682785511,0.00670646084472537,-0.01198763307183981,-0.021814648061990738,-0.016504792496562004,0.019785277545452118,-0.012073623016476631,0.0023794739972800016,0.011244717985391617,0.018489418551325798,0.012051289901137352,0.02614659257233143,-0.008627600036561489,SageMaker Inference Pipeline with Preprocessing,"How to deploy an ML model and its associated data preprocessing logic together as a single, unified endpoint for real-time inference, ensuring consistency between training and serving.","Real-time ML inference scenarios where input data requires specific transformations (e.g., scaling, encoding, feature engineering) before being fed to the model, and these transformations should be part of the serving endpoint to prevent skew.","Create an Amazon SageMaker inference pipeline that chains together multiple containers: one for preprocessing (e.g., using a custom script or SageMaker Processing job output) and another for the ML model itself. This pipeline is then deployed as a single endpoint.","A robust and consistent real-time inference endpoint where preprocessing steps are executed automatically as part of the model invocation, reducing operational complexity and preventing data skew issues.",Deploying models that require complex feature engineering; ensuring consistent data transformations between training and inference; simplifying endpoint management.,
