96996754408,-0.0023862645030021667,0.016486134380102158,0.0013762757880613208,0.0004067976260557771,-0.0018247162224724889,0.0033381639514118433,0.010728482156991959,0.004074510652571917,-0.004214825574308634,-0.013950946740806103,0.015516024082899094,-0.02971268631517887,-0.003989037126302719,-0.022349681705236435,0.0036924376618117094,0.014979612082242966,0.03896555304527283,-0.002224716590717435,Distributed Feature Engineering for Large-Scale ML Datasets,How to perform feature engineering on extremely large (terabyte-scale) machine learning datasets efficiently and scalably.,"ML projects dealing with big data where traditional single-machine processing is infeasible, and feature engineering requires distributed computing.","Utilize Amazon SageMaker Processing, a managed service for running data processing workloads, to execute distributed feature engineering scripts (e.g., using Spark, scikit-learn, or custom containers) on terabyte-scale datasets.","Scalable and efficient preparation of large datasets for ML model training, enabling the development of models on previously unmanageable data volumes.",Preparing massive datasets for training; transforming raw data into features; cleaning data at scale.,
