7553,0.008483976125717163,0.010565357282757759,0.020043157041072845,0.01588498428463936,-0.0016756551340222359,0.006343542598187923,0.009685780853033066,0.012852453626692295,0.007865034975111485,-0.011718526482582092,-0.01998639479279518,-0.0039324467070400715,0.012909652665257454,-0.02245417796075344,-0.006218306254595518,0.0038234598468989134,0.0052336435765028,0.03182601183652878,0.03138016536831856,-0.02025323547422886,Cold Start Time Series Forecasting with DeepAR,"Traditional time series forecasting methods (e.g., ARIMA, ETS) are ineffective for 'cold start' scenarios where a new product or entity has little to no historical data, leading to inaccurate predictions.","Forecasting scalar one-dimensional time series for new items or products that have minimal historical data, but are part of a larger dataset containing hundreds of related time series.","Employ a supervised learning algorithm like DeepAR (based on recurrent neural networks) that trains a single model jointly over all related time series. For cold products, an iterative approach is used: start with a new model with an initial context length defined by available historical points, and progressively retrain or update the model as more data points are acquired, increasing the context length until it reaches the desired prediction length. Hyperparameter tuning is used to find the best model.","Accurate forecasts for cold start items by leveraging patterns learned from related time series, even with limited historical data for the specific item. The model's prediction accuracy improves as more historical data becomes available.","New product sales forecasting, web traffic forecasting for new services, patient demand anticipation for new medical procedures, resource allocation for new initiatives.",
