80726930499077,0.01598506048321724,0.005596301984041929,0.013353901915252209,-8.018814696697518e-05,-0.00821705162525177,-0.019490275532007217,0.008724886924028397,0.005081474781036377,0.006751158740371466,-0.009056832641363144,-0.02471659518778324,0.015235699713230133,-0.004329455550760031,-0.013496252708137035,-0.020730799064040184,0.004761403892189264,0.015628715977072716,0.029520375654101372,-0.0006821599090471864,Cross-Cloud MLOps Workflow,"Organizations often have existing DevOps tools (e.g., Azure DevOps) and data storage solutions in one cloud, but prefer to use ML services (e.g., Amazon SageMaker) in another cloud, requiring integration and automation of the ML lifecycle across these platforms.","Building, training, deploying, monitoring, and retraining ML models systematically and repeatedly, while leveraging existing infrastructure and tools across different cloud providers (e.g., Azure for CI/CD, AWS for ML). Applicable to FMOps and LLMOps.","Integrate Azure DevOps pipelines for Continuous Integration (CI) and Continuous Deployment (CD) with Amazon SageMaker for ML model development, training, fine-tuning, evaluation, and deployment. The CI (Model Build Pipeline) triggers SageMaker pipelines for training and model registration. The CD (Model Deploy Pipeline) is triggered by model approval in SageMaker Model Registry to deploy to staging and production, including monitoring setup. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is used for environment provisioning.","An efficient, automated, and scalable ML workflow that spans multiple cloud platforms, ensuring faster deployment, better accuracy over time, and robust operationalization of ML models, including generative AI models.","Operationalizing ML models in hybrid/multi-cloud environments, FMOps, LLMOps, ensuring governance and best practices across the ML lifecycle.",
