97,-0.004638150334358215,0.013873424381017685,0.019726619124412537,-0.0036579042207449675,0.01168377511203289,0.007527215871959925,0.006641922518610954,-0.012417778372764587,0.012584365904331207,0.012103176675736904,-0.010726043954491615,-0.02160760387778282,-0.004498790018260479,0.018553543835878372,-0.023346958681941032,0.0032319871243089437,-0.004143382888287306,0.0012568329693749547,0.006587012205272913,0.027586668729782104,-0.02030034363269806,Custom Container for SageMaker ML Training,"Data scientists need to use custom algorithms, specific programming languages, frameworks, or dependencies that are not natively supported by standard SageMaker environments for model training.",Developing and training machine learning models in Amazon SageMaker where the required software stack or algorithm is highly specialized or not available in pre-built SageMaker images.,"Create a custom Docker container image that includes the specific algorithms, libraries, and dependencies needed for the SageMaker processing job. Store this Docker image in a container registry (e.g., Amazon ECR). Then, define a SageMaker processing step within an orchestration service (e.g., AWS Step Functions) that references this custom Docker image and executes the custom Python training script. The container exports the trained model to an S3 bucket.","The ability to run virtually any custom code or ML algorithm within the SageMaker environment, providing flexibility and control over the training environment, and integrating it into automated ML workflows.","Training models with niche libraries, custom-built algorithms, specific versions of frameworks, or non-standard programming languages in SageMaker.",
