17327865585684776,0.015081432648003101,0.024072542786598206,0.004337616730481386,0.014362536370754242,-0.018224434927105904,0.0200617965310812,0.0017003758111968637,0.00010240454867016524,-0.01149685587733984,-0.0175932664424181,0.02948620170354843,-0.02090604417026043,-0.013947675935924053,0.003309444757178426,-0.0014778299955651164,0.00665702810510993,0.030286602675914764,-0.018676921725273132,Agentic EKS Access Management,"Managing access controls and resource provisioning for multiple teams working with a shared Amazon EKS cluster is administratively complex, time-consuming, and prone to manual errors.","Streamlining Amazon EKS cluster administration, particularly for access management (creating user access entries, managing access policies, configuring pod identity associations), by enabling natural language interaction.","Implement an Amazon Bedrock agent configured with action groups (backed by AWS Lambda functions) and a knowledge base (e.g., Amazon OpenSearch Service indexed with EKS User Guide content from S3). Users submit natural language prompts to the agent. The agent interprets the prompt, identifies the relevant API operation via an OpenAPI schema, or queries the knowledge base for contextual information. For actionable requests, the agent triggers the appropriate Lambda function to perform the EKS access management task (e.g., create-access-entry, associate-access-policy, delete-access-entry).","Simplified Amazon EKS cluster administration through natural language prompts, reduced manual overhead, improved development efficiency, and automated management of access policies and pod identities.","Automated infrastructure management, self-service IT operations, conversational interfaces for cloud resource management, reducing administrative burden for complex systems.",
