3,-0.007427701260894537,0.02364134043455124,0.014773137867450714,0.015492155216634274,0.021926913410425186,-0.013198948465287685,0.008645737543702126,0.007884188555181026,0.01991093158721924,0.013752108439803123,-0.0015690368600189686,-0.0245388001203537,-0.017262397333979607,0.0076697515323758125,-0.04010891541838646,0.0005148031050339341,-0.0015885287430137396,-0.0034786907490342855,0.017778465524315834,0.02509739249944687,-0.01363333873450756,Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with Vector Store,"Large Language Models (LLMs) may lack up-to-date, domain-specific, or private information, leading to generic, outdated, or hallucinated responses.","Building generative AI applications that require LLMs to provide accurate, contextually relevant, and grounded responses based on proprietary or external knowledge sources, with low latency for document ingestion and retrieval.","Implement a RAG-based application where: 1. Users upload documents (e.g., PDF, Excel) to a storage service (e.g., Amazon S3). 2. Content is extracted, chunked, and embedded into a vector store (e.g., Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL-Compatible with pgvector). This enables near real-time ingestion. 3. When a user queries the text generation model (e.g., via Amazon Bedrock), the query is first used to retrieve relevant document chunks from the vector store. 4. These retrieved chunks are then provided as context to the LLM, augmenting its generation capabilities. LangChain can be used to orchestrate this workflow.","LLM responses are enhanced with relevant, accurate, and up-to-date information from the specified knowledge base, reducing hallucinations and improving the quality and specificity of generated text.","Enterprise chatbots, intelligent document Q&A, personalized content generation, research assistants, any application requiring LLMs to interact with external, dynamic, or private data.",
