26215663552284,0.018098004162311554,0.00021272395679261535,0.01621931418776512,-0.0045308698900043964,0.006422718055546284,0.000754278153181076,0.019467130303382874,0.009916504845023155,-0.0020828580018132925,-0.011149857193231583,-0.006335604935884476,0.00914154201745987,-0.03398945927619934,-0.0073884460143744946,-0.005835718475282192,0.003755922894924879,0.018960891291499138,0.0212986059486866,-0.010111192241311073,Model Invocation Logging for Generative AI,"Building robust generative AI applications requires collecting invocation logs, model input data, and model output data for all model invocations to enable monitoring, auditing, and debugging.","Developing and operating generative AI applications using Foundation Models (FMs) in a managed service like Amazon Bedrock, where detailed logging of interactions is crucial for operational visibility, compliance, and performance analysis.","Configure the generative AI service (e.g., Amazon Bedrock) to automatically collect model invocation logs, including input and output data. Store these logs in centralized logging services (e.g., Amazon CloudWatch Logs for real-time monitoring, custom metrics, and alarms) and/or long-term storage (e.g., Amazon S3 for replication, long-term archiving, and data lake integration). Infrastructure as Code (IaC) like AWS CloudFormation can be used to provision and manage the logging infrastructure (log groups, S3 buckets, KMS keys, IAM roles).","Comprehensive logging of all generative AI model invocations, enabling monitoring, auditing, debugging, creating custom metrics and alarms, and ensuring compliance and data governance for AI applications.","Auditing AI model usage, debugging prompt engineering issues, monitoring model performance, compliance requirements, data governance for sensitive AI interactions, creating custom dashboards for generative AI applications.",
