04115804284811,-0.004622995387762785,-0.001642269198782742,0.008069013245403767,0.003512080293148756,0.029311906546354294,0.01704922318458557,0.010760563425719738,-0.018466684967279434,0.017838232219219208,0.02991420030593872,0.010596944019198418,-0.019448887556791306,-0.023344265297055244,0.008186260238289833,-0.017784718424081802,-0.007370414212346077,-0.0069252680987119675,0.006771760061383247,0.01423539500683546,0.013828955590724945,1.244899885932682e-05,Realtime AI-Assisted Code Security Validation,"AI code generators can introduce security vulnerabilities or misconfigurations, creating a 'security blind spot.' Developers need immediate feedback on security issues during code generation to address them early.","When developers use AI coding assistants (e.g., Kiro, Amazon Q Developer, Cline) to generate or analyze code and Infrastructure as Code (IaC), and there's a need to ensure the security and compliance of the generated output in real-time.","An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server integrates multiple industry-standard security scanning tools (e.g., Checkov, Semgrep, Bandit). AI coding assistants send code snippets or IaC configurations to this server for security scanning. The server routes the request to the appropriate specialized scanner, and the results (findings, severity, descriptions, fixes) are sent back to the developer through the AI assistant in real-time.","Developers receive immediate security feedback during code generation, enabling them to identify and address potential security vulnerabilities, misconfigurations, and compliance violations early in the development process. This bridges the gap between AI efficiency and security compliance.","Secure software development, IaC security, continuous security scanning in development workflows.",
