7857460976,0.021487703546881676,0.02506120316684246,-0.005466621369123459,0.00574319576844573,0.00018382746202405542,0.010959255509078503,0.01701273024082184,-0.008227498270571232,-0.017481764778494835,-0.019672468304634094,0.007420791778713465,-0.016668930649757385,-0.0027972920797765255,-0.0006045909831300378,-0.009121856652200222,0.02855806052684784,0.032868437469005585,-0.02667379565536976,Intent Classification for Chatbots,"Chat-based assistants need to understand the user's goal or purpose behind a query to route it to the appropriate processing workflow or service. Without this, a single LLM might struggle to handle diverse types of requests efficiently and accurately.","When designing a chat-based assistant that needs to handle a variety of user inquiries, some requiring general knowledge, others specific data retrieval, and some complex multi-step reasoning.","The input query from the user is first classified into one of several predefined intents (e.g., 'General SageMaker guidance questions,' 'General SageMaker pricing training/inference questions,' 'Complex questions related to SageMaker and pricing'). Based on the classified intent, the query is then routed to a specific backend service or workflow optimized for that type of request (e.g., RAG service, Database Query service, Incontext ReACT Agent service).","Improves the efficiency and accuracy of chat-based assistants by ensuring that queries are handled by the most appropriate and specialized backend logic, leading to more relevant and targeted responses.","Chatbots, virtual assistants, customer service automation, conversational AI.",
