895411372185,0.016786564141511917,0.0153279397636652,0.003722656285390258,0.016151579096913338,-0.010774689726531506,0.0056860921904444695,-0.0008242751937359571,0.014539247378706932,0.0004933500895276666,-0.015217543579638004,-0.02362946607172489,-0.015865208581089973,0.0020156227983534336,-0.03424493968486786,-0.011215423233807087,-0.007332965265959501,-0.0024229991249740124,0.012069049291312695,0.03151591494679451,-0.018728436902165413,Prompt Engineering for Grounding and Factuality,"Large Language Models (LLMs) can generate inaccurate, ungrounded, or hallucinated information, especially when dealing with specific factual queries or sensitive domains.","When designing prompts for LLMs where the accuracy, factuality, and adherence to provided context (grounding) are critical, and the goal is to minimize fabricated or misleading responses.",Carefully craft prompts that explicitly instruct the LLM to: only use information provided in the context; state when it cannot find an answer in the provided context; avoid making up information; and emphasize the importance of factual accuracy. This is described as 'careful prompt engineering to minimize inaccuracies and make sure that responses are anchored in factual documentation'.,Improves the trustworthiness and reliability of LLM outputs by reducing hallucinations and ensuring responses are anchored in factual documentation or provided context.,"Factual question-answering, legal/medical AI, enterprise knowledge systems, any application where accuracy is paramount.",
