8,0.008202053606510162,0.01872975192964077,0.012536386959254742,0.03150901198387146,0.0026030177250504494,0.00950089655816555,-0.00139245658647269,0.009808746166527271,0.01965022273361683,-0.004700428806245327,-0.010315677151083946,-0.0243064071983099,0.008046635426580906,-0.0344574898481369,-0.0013861125335097313,0.006876640021800995,0.005535837262868881,0.0011280308244749904,0.011646251194179058,-0.017808904871344566,Visualize AIML Model Results with Web UI,"Visualizing output from AI/ML services often requires complex API calls and custom development, making it difficult for analysts to quickly explore new datasets or interact with model results.","Need to enhance the accessibility of AI/ML services and provide a more interactive form of data analysis for users (e.g., analysts) who want to upload their own data and visualize model results in a dashboard.","Integrate an AI service (e.g., Amazon Comprehend) or a custom ML model endpoint with a custom web application (e.g., Flask) and deploy it using a platform like AWS Elastic Beanstalk. The web application allows users to upload data, sends it for inference, and visualizes the results (e.g., sentiments, entities) in a dashboard using libraries like Plotly.","A web-based user interface that enables users to upload data, get model inferences, and visualize results interactively, making AI/ML services more accessible.","Visualizing sentiment analysis and named entity recognition from user-provided text data using Amazon Comprehend, adapting to other AWS AI services or custom trained models hosted on endpoints (e.g., SageMaker endpoint).",
