.0007912214496172965,-0.010271153412759304,0.007867581211030483,0.010218809358775616,0.011519985273480415,-0.013594239950180054,-0.010871872305870056,0.015394385904073715,0.010120682418346405,0.011340837925672531,-0.018201230093836784,-0.014145193621516228,0.02720256708562374,-0.01537685003131628,0.0010249506449326873,-0.006512463092803955,-0.005874681286513805,-0.002654250944033265,0.03770707547664642,-0.009450145997107029,Scalable Value at Risk (VaR) Calculation,"How to efficiently perform computationally intensive Value at Risk (VaR) calculations, which involve numerous mathematical and statistical operations, requiring dynamic scalability to handle unpredictable batch or real-time processing loads within service-level agreements.","Financial institutions or risk management departments needing to calculate VaR for portfolios, where input data (e.g., trade data, market data) can arrive as streams or batches. The calculations are often independent for different tasks, allowing for parallelization.","A serverless architecture is employed. Trade data streams into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. AWS Lambda functions process these orders, netting positions and writing consolidated messages for each ticker to an Amazon SQS risk queue. Another set of Lambda functions, acting as the risk calculation engine, consume messages from SQS, perform the complex VaR calculations (potentially using simulated ticker price series data), and update VaR/PnL information in an Amazon ElastiCache risk cache. Finally, a Lambda function retrieves results from ElastiCache and stores them in a database (e.g., Amazon Aurora MySQL-Compatible) and S3 for persistence and reporting. The system leverages automatic scaling of Lambda functions and SQS queues to adapt to varying compute demands.","A highly scalable, reliable, and cost-optimized system for VaR calculations that can process large volumes of data in real-time or batch, dynamically adjusting compute resources to meet performance requirements and minimize costs.","Financial risk management, quantitative finance, large-scale statistical modeling, simulation-based analysis, computational finance.",
