414444,-0.01368071511387825,0.010167475789785385,0.0011599978897720575,-0.011162994429469109,0.01126574445515871,-0.001144691719673574,-0.0019092452712357044,-0.014228438958525658,0.011859290301799774,0.016839882358908653,0.005940411239862442,0.0032507898285984993,-0.01742979884147644,0.011184249073266983,-0.02284673973917961,0.009134278632700443,-0.020108703523874283,0.005643368232995272,0.005181157495826483,0.03679054602980614,-0.0010226871818304062,Generate Synthetic Test Data for ML Workflows,"How to efficiently create large-scale, structured test datasets for evaluating the performance and scalability of data processing and machine learning pipelines, especially when real data is unavailable, insufficient, or sensitive.","Developing, testing, and benchmarking data-intensive applications, including those that prepare data for or consume data from machine learning models. There is a need to simulate real-world data volumes and structures to validate system behavior and performance.","Utilize a serverless ETL service (like AWS Glue) to programmatically generate a large number of structured data files (e.g., CSV) with random content. These files are stored in an object storage service (like Amazon S3). The generation process can be parallelized using job parameters (e.g., STARTRANGE, ENDRANGE) to control file naming and quantity, allowing for scalable data creation.","Enables rapid creation of millions of sample files, facilitating performance testing, scalability evaluation, and troubleshooting of data pipelines and downstream analytical or machine learning services. Reduces cost and time by allowing local development and testing with smaller datasets before scaling.","Testing the performance of AWS Glue Studio or AWS Glue DataBrew jobs, benchmarking data analysis pipelines, creating synthetic datasets for ML model training or inference testing, load testing ML data pipelines.",
