68,-0.009693179279565811,0.014581888914108276,0.017920760437846184,0.008588127791881561,0.005792513955384493,0.001056704786606133,-0.00707401754334569,-0.018697774037718773,0.0007131103775463998,0.008523557335138321,0.0024233327712863684,-0.01148757804185152,-0.013152902014553547,0.014099358581006527,-0.01954001747071743,0.004512244835495949,-0.005961488001048565,0.006129560060799122,0.011787215247750282,0.04019332677125931,-0.0040364754386246204,Transient EMR Cluster for Batch ML Processing,"How to cost-effectively and scalably execute batch processing jobs, particularly those involving big data frameworks like Spark, for machine learning workflows, ensuring resources are only consumed when needed.","Running computationally intensive batch jobs (e.g., data preparation, feature engineering, model training, batch inference) that require a distributed computing environment (like Apache Spark) but do not need a continuously running cluster.","Use a serverless function (AWS Lambda) to trigger the Amazon EMR RunJobFlow API action. This launches a transient EMR cluster configured to run a specific Spark job. The cluster is designed to automatically terminate upon job completion or failure, optimizing cost and resource utilization. Input data and output results are stored in object storage (Amazon S3).","Cost savings due to on-demand resource allocation, scalability and flexibility in executing big data computations, and automated resource management. Enables efficient execution of batch ML tasks without maintaining persistent infrastructure.","Batch feature engineering, batch model training, large-scale data preprocessing for ML, batch inference, data aggregation for ML dashboards.",
