.0005615431000478566,0.02316645346581936,0.018130242824554443,0.006351099349558353,0.023980718106031418,-0.013052460737526417,-0.004920995328575373,0.0015064348699524999,0.009721243754029274,0.027110297232866287,0.00874546729028225,0.007479339372366667,0.0021228177938610315,0.011966738849878311,-0.035220008343458176,0.0006034159450791776,-0.003063833573833108,-0.0015509186778217554,0.010011337697505951,0.017256611958146095,-0.022795500233769417,Amazon Redshift ML for Advanced Analytics,"Database users need to perform machine learning analytics on data stored in Amazon Redshift or S3, but lack the specialized ML expertise or tools to easily create, train, and deploy ML models.","Data resides in an Amazon Redshift cluster or Amazon S3. Users are familiar with standard SQL commands. The need is to perform supervised learning tasks (e.g., regression, binary classification, multiclass classification) for use cases like revenue forecasting, credit card fraud detection, customer lifetime value (CLV), or customer churn predictions. The Redshift cluster and S3 bucket must be in the same AWS Region.","Leverage Amazon Redshift ML, which integrates with Amazon SageMaker Autopilot. Database users can create, train, and deploy ML models using standard SQL commands (e.g., CREATE MODEL statement). Amazon Redshift ML abstracts away the complexities of interacting with Amazon S3 and SageMaker. SageMaker Autopilot automatically preprocesses training data, searches for and recommends optimal ML algorithms, and tunes hyperparameters. The trained and deployed ML model is then registered as a user-defined function (UDF) in Amazon Redshift.","ML models can be easily created, trained, and deployed by database users using familiar SQL, without requiring deep ML expertise. Predictions can be made directly within SQL queries using the ML model UDF. Automated model training and tuning by SageMaker Autopilot ensures optimal models for classification or regression tasks. This enables advanced analytics use cases directly within the data warehouse.","Revenue forecasting, credit card fraud detection, customer lifetime value (CLV) prediction, customer churn prediction, and any supervised learning task (regression, binary classification, multiclass classification) on data in Redshift/S3.",
