45685338974,0.019223392009735107,0.008815940469503403,0.015173200517892838,-0.0013347616186365485,-0.0014322526985779405,-0.0044176010414958,0.007038970943540335,0.02482500672340393,0.008871565572917461,0.002600521082058549,-0.005312751512974501,0.009575103409588337,-0.031490810215473175,-0.007217266131192446,-0.00035596470115706325,0.004448146093636751,0.008067401126027107,0.021810853853821754,-0.01631150208413601,Automated ML Model Training and Deployment (Redshift ML),"Data analysts and scientists need an easy way to build, train, and deploy ML models directly from their data warehouse without deep ML expertise, and then use these models for inference via SQL.","An organization uses Amazon Redshift as its data warehouse and wants to leverage supervised machine learning (regression, binary classification, multiclass classification) on its data. They require automation for the complex steps of ML model development and seamless integration for inference.","The pattern involves using Amazon Redshift ML, which integrates with Amazon SageMaker Autopilot. Amazon Redshift exports training data to an S3 bucket. SageMaker Autopilot automatically preprocesses the training data, searches for and recommends the optimal ML algorithm and hyperparameters, and trains the model. Amazon Redshift ML then registers the output ML model as a SQL function within the Redshift cluster, making it available for use in SQL statements.","ML models are automatically built, trained, and deployed, significantly reducing the need for specialized ML expertise. Inference can be performed directly within the data warehouse using standard SQL, making ML accessible to a broader range of users (data scientists, business intelligence users).",Predicting customer churn directly from customer activity data in Redshift; classifying transactions for fraud detection; generating product recommendations based on user behavior stored in the data warehouse; any supervised learning task where data resides in Redshift and the goal is to simplify and automate the ML lifecycle from training to inference.,
