41682934761,0.026149807497859,-0.008221718482673168,0.013446621596813202,-0.00015862446161918342,-0.001929995371028781,-0.011135291308164597,0.004407207015901804,0.002530344994738698,0.012259704992175102,0.0014048423618078232,-0.011088104918599129,0.038059134036302567,-0.03141177073121071,-0.008038198575377464,-0.012137848883867264,0.021690210327506065,0.010870596393942833,0.025580059736967087,0.004255617968738079,Cross-Account CodeCommit Access for SageMaker Notebooks,"Securely providing SageMaker notebook instances with temporary access to source code repositories (e.g., CodeCommit) located in different AWS accounts, while adhering to least privilege principles, can be complex.","Data scientists and ML engineers often work in separate development accounts and need to access shared code repositories for model development, training scripts, or data processing logic, which might reside in a central code repository account.","Implement an IAM role and trust policy configuration that allows the SageMaker notebook instance's execution role in one account to assume a role in the CodeCommit account, granting temporary, scoped access to the repository.","Enhanced security and simplified access management for SageMaker notebook instances to cross-account CodeCommit repositories, promoting collaboration while maintaining isolation and compliance.","Secure ML development, collaborative ML projects, managing code for ML models across accounts, enforcing security best practices in ML environments.",
