08943017572164536,0.024152541533112526,-0.001258243340998888,0.017468946054577827,0.03161509707570076,-0.00772136589512229,-0.0064900582656264305,0.02451888844370842,0.009144277311861515,-0.0013916592579334974,-0.013467223383486271,-0.025132376700639725,0.008051303215324879,-0.00794997252523899,0.0003783517749980092,0.0013922958169132471,-0.001133498502895236,-0.004156346432864666,0.01923573575913906,-0.007900169119238853,Edge AI Containerization with Docker-in-Docker,"AWS IoT Greengrass V2, when deployed as a Docker container, does not natively support running other Docker application containers (including those hosting AI/ML models) within its environment. This restricts the flexibility and scalability of deploying containerized AI applications at the edge.","Edge computing environments where AI/ML inference needs to be performed close to data sources (e.g., IoT devices, industrial equipment) to minimize latency, conserve bandwidth, and ensure operation in disconnected scenarios. AWS IoT Greengrass V2 is used as the edge runtime, deployed as a Docker container on a host server.","Create a custom Docker image for AWS IoT Greengrass V2 that incorporates Docker-in-Docker (DinD) functionality. This custom image allows the Greengrass core to orchestrate and run additional containerized applications, such as AI/ML inference models, as nested Docker containers. This approach maintains full Greengrass V2 functionality, including AWS IoT SiteWise Edge processing, while enabling scalable, container-based deployments for AI workloads.","Enables the flexible and scalable deployment of containerized AI/ML applications on edge devices managed by AWS IoT Greengrass V2, even when Greengrass itself is running as a container. Facilitates local data processing and AI inference at the edge, with seamless integration for sending processed data to cloud services for further analysis and storage.","Deploying computer vision models for quality control on a factory floor, running predictive maintenance algorithms on industrial machinery, real-time anomaly detection on sensor data at the edge using containerized ML models.",
