172531,-0.00285362615250051,0.006454853340983391,0.00556638278067112,-0.01262031402438879,-0.014528203755617142,0.015520745888352394,0.01196066290140152,-0.009499653242528439,-0.02166822925209999,-0.018625792115926743,0.017925696447491646,-0.014906478114426136,0.002393060829490423,0.006358635611832142,0.012729786336421967,0.011157656088471413,0.024558160454034805,-0.013646407052874565,SageMaker Inference Pipeline for Preprocessing,"Managing separate services for data preprocessing and ML model inference, leading to increased latency, operational overhead, and potential inconsistencies between training and serving environments.","An ML model requires specific preprocessing steps (e.g., scaling, encoding, feature engineering) before making predictions, and these steps need to be consistently applied during inference.",Package the preprocessing logic and the ML model into a single Amazon SageMaker inference pipeline. This allows the preprocessing steps to be executed sequentially with the model inference within a single endpoint.,"Reduced inference latency, simplified deployment and management of ML models with preprocessing, ensured consistency between training and serving, and improved operational efficiency.","Deploying ML models that require feature transformation, data normalization, text vectorization, or image preprocessing as part of the real-time inference process.",
