2165,0.011288125067949295,0.00950341671705246,0.0033432289492338896,0.015169183723628521,-0.0057993861846625805,0.0056701041758060455,0.0027099070139229298,0.01939632184803486,0.022332781925797462,0.004719909746199846,-0.015533611178398132,-0.023397846147418022,0.00556984543800354,-0.029943281784653664,-0.007685589138418436,-0.009778289124369621,-0.004001593217253685,0.014729784801602364,0.02360500954091549,-0.010296101681888103,Deploy a RAG use case on AWS by using Terraform and Amazon Bedrock,"How to build generative AI applications that can access and synthesize information from proprietary or external knowledge sources beyond their initial training data, ensuring factual accuracy and reducing hallucinations.","Developers want to create LLM-powered applications (e.g., chatbots, Q&A systems) that provide contextually relevant and accurate responses by grounding the LLM's generation in specific, up-to-date information.","Implement a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture on AWS. This involves using Amazon Bedrock for the LLM, a vector database (e.g., Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Aurora with pgvector) to store and retrieve relevant documents, and orchestrating the workflow with tools like Terraform for infrastructure as code. The process typically includes: 1. Ingesting and embedding documents into a vector store. 2. Retrieving relevant document chunks based on user queries. 3. Augmenting the LLM prompt with the retrieved context. 4. Generating a response using the LLM on Amazon Bedrock.","A generative AI application capable of providing accurate, context-aware, and grounded responses by leveraging external knowledge bases, reducing reliance on the LLM's pre-trained knowledge.","Building intelligent chatbots, enterprise search, personalized content generation, factual Q&A systems.",
