0.02005002647638321,-0.010269852355122566,0.025364942848682404,0.002135040471330285,-0.00129139784257859,-0.012916975654661655,0.01842397265136242,0.02245360054075718,0.0254617128521204,-0.0075788977555930614,-0.007813715375959873,-0.0011585030006244779,-0.021722937002778053,0.002178051508963108,-0.010898970998823643,0.015346677042543888,0.006873368285596371,0.009205429814755917,-0.00294140400364995,Sensitive Data Identification for AI Artifacts,"Sensitive data may be present in various AI-specific data artifacts, such as knowledge bases, model invocation logs, and prompt stores, leading to privacy, compliance, and security risks.","Organizations deploying AI/ML models, especially those involving Large Language Models (LLMs) or knowledge-intensive AI systems, need to ensure that sensitive information within their operational data (e.g., model inputs/outputs, prompts, and underlying knowledge bases) is identified and protected. These artifacts are typically stored in cloud storage services like Amazon S3.","Utilize a data discovery and classification service (e.g., Amazon Macie) to automatically scan and identify sensitive data within AI-specific storage locations, including knowledge bases used as data sources, model invocation logs, and prompt stores.","Proactive identification and protection of sensitive data across AI-related assets, enhancing data privacy, ensuring compliance with regulations, and reducing the overall security exposure of AI systems.","Ensuring compliance with data protection regulations (e.g., GDPR, HIPAA), preventing accidental data leaks from AI systems, improving the security posture of AI applications, and auditing the content of AI-generated or AI-consumed data.",
