5,0.01232568733394146,0.004074615426361561,0.026853758841753006,-0.011763105168938637,-0.007055230438709259,-0.0030348754953593016,0.025468965992331505,0.0005325818201527,-3.676917185657658e-05,-0.010676243342459202,-0.007843165658414364,0.012546293437480927,-0.04720839112997055,0.005609951913356781,-0.005964044481515884,-0.005273060407489538,3.4054432035190985e-05,0.035503875464200974,-0.03225532919168472,Natural Language Querying for Business Intelligence,"Business users need to quickly retrieve specific data insights or answers to ad-hoc questions from a BI platform without needing to write complex queries (e.g., SQL) or navigate intricate BI tool interfaces.","Business data is integrated into a BI service (e.g., Amazon Quick Sight) that is augmented with generative AI capabilities (e.g., Amazon Q). Users have access to a natural language interface within the BI tool.","Users input their data-related questions or requests using natural language prompts (e.g., 'Show member distribution by region', 'Show members not completed preventive immunization'). The integrated AI service processes these prompts, understands the intent, and translates them into appropriate data retrieval and analysis operations within the BI platform, presenting the results (which could be raw data, summaries, or visuals).","Empowers non-technical users to perform self-service data exploration and obtain immediate answers to business questions, reducing reliance on data analysts and accelerating decision-making.","Asking ad-hoc questions about data distributions, identifying specific segments of data, querying for trends, and getting quick summaries without manual report building.",
