7011384367943,0.01715928502380848,-0.007145958486944437,0.004726069048047066,-0.0036855898797512054,-0.01299795787781477,-0.016466427594423294,0.008339009247720242,-0.002011663978919387,0.008340412750840187,-0.011689556762576103,-0.007909663952887058,0.029567373916506767,-0.018960418179631233,-0.0013588863657787442,-0.010095994919538498,0.005116096697747707,0.00290960562415421,0.031654901802539825,-0.015073707327246666,CloudWatch Anomaly Detection for Custom Metrics,"Traditional static thresholds for monitoring metrics are insufficient to detect subtle or dynamic operational issues, leading to missed anomalies or alert fatigue.","Monitoring custom metrics (e.g., API response times) in a cloud environment where 'normal' operating windows can be dynamic and complex.","Utilize Amazon CloudWatch's anomaly detection feature to establish dynamic thresholds based on past patterns of the custom metrics. This involves creating a custom metric (via Lambda or Log Insights) and then configuring an alarm with anomaly detection, which automatically updates its band and thresholds as more data is aggregated.","Proactive notification of metrics falling outside the normal operating window, preventing SLA breaches and improving operational performance by identifying true anomalies rather than static threshold breaches.","Monitoring API response times, identifying unusual traffic patterns, detecting performance degradation, and general operational monitoring where dynamic baselining is required.",
