095,0.001676781801506877,0.004357682075351477,0.013039304874837399,-0.00737087382003665,0.010534146800637245,-0.006897933781147003,-0.006771461572498083,-0.025046193972229958,0.022730562835931778,0.003829368157312274,0.015386906452476978,0.0002682782069314271,-0.01016700454056263,0.015836719423532486,-0.018475467339158058,-0.012327517382800579,-0.013504406437277794,0.002239407040178776,0.005741046741604805,0.031181007623672485,-0.017090274021029472,Multi-Account/Region AIOps with Amazon DevOps Guru,"Manually monitoring and troubleshooting operational issues across a complex, distributed cloud environment (multiple accounts, regions, OUs) is time-consuming, error-prone, and requires significant manual effort and ML expertise.","Managing and monitoring application availability and performance across a large-scale AWS environment, where operational data is vast and anomalies can be subtle or complex to diagnose.","Deploy Amazon DevOps Guru across the organization (multiple accounts, regions, OUs) using AWS CDK. DevOps Guru automatically ingests operational data, baselines resource behavior, applies ML-powered anomaly detection, correlates events from various sources (e.g., CloudWatch, CloudTrail), and generates actionable insights with recommendations. SNS notifications alert operators to detected anomalies.","Improved application availability, faster resolution of operational issues, reduced manual effort, and ML-powered recommendations without requiring in-house ML expertise.","Proactive detection and diagnosis of operational issues, performance degradation, resource misconfigurations, and other anomalies in complex cloud applications, especially for large organizations.",
