05006053019315004,0.012745066545903683,-0.0016124051762744784,-0.0040901051834225655,-0.011757045984268188,0.004913907032459974,0.0015409965999424458,0.010983956046402454,8.558554691262543e-05,-0.009071893990039825,0.03876513987779617,-0.0307233277708292,-0.008167965337634087,-0.014789676293730736,0.01642671786248684,0.00974175613373518,0.02669586054980755,0.008580872789025307,Cross-Account Secure Code Access for SageMaker,"ML developers using Amazon SageMaker notebook instances in one AWS account need secure, temporary, and auditable access to source code repositories (like AWS CodeCommit) that are centrally managed in a different AWS account, without granting overly broad or permanent permissions.","A multi-account AWS environment where ML development and experimentation (using SageMaker) are separated from core source code management (using CodeCommit) for security, governance, or organizational structure reasons. Developers require seamless access to code for model training, feature engineering, or script development.","Configure AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles and policies to enable SageMaker notebook instances in a consumer account to assume a role in the creator account, granting temporary, least-privilege access to specific CodeCommit repositories. This typically involves trust policies, resource policies, and potentially AWS STS for temporary credentials.","Enhanced security posture by adhering to the principle of least privilege and temporary access, improved governance over code access, and streamlined collaboration for ML development across organizational boundaries within AWS.","Allowing SageMaker notebooks to clone, pull, or push code from/to CodeCommit repositories in a different account for ML project development, version control, and collaboration.",
