075718969107,-0.0030620130710303783,0.016264161095023155,-0.011889235116541386,0.006376518402248621,0.009132358245551586,-0.005165736656636,-0.026941198855638504,0.00154836755245924,0.002688364824280143,0.012302115559577942,-0.00040204968536272645,-0.014034965075552464,0.009260527789592743,-0.03248371556401253,0.004596972372382879,-0.009291199967265129,0.00947056245058775,-0.006761642638593912,0.008372833020985126,0.00717260641977191,Dynamic Least-Privilege Policy Generation,Implementing least-privilege access in an already active AWS account can be challenging because you don't want to unintentionally block users from performing their job duties by changing their permissions. Understanding the specific actions and resources performed by account users is difficult and time-consuming.,"An active AWS account with AWS CloudTrail enabled, where IAM roles need to be updated to reflect least-privilege access based on actual usage, without disrupting team productivity. The goal is to generate an up-to-date IAM policy for a role based on its current activity.","Utilize AWS IAM Access Analyzer to analyze AWS CloudTrail logs for activity within a specified date range for a given IAM role. IAM Access Analyzer generates an IAM policy that permits only the actions and services used by the role during that period. This process is orchestrated by AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda, allowing for integration of custom allow/deny rules. The generated policy is then stored in an AWS CodeCommit repository for subsequent deployment via a CI/CD pipeline.","Automatically generated, up-to-date IAM policies that enforce the principle of least-privilege access, removing unnecessary elevated privileges and improving the security posture of the AWS environment without extensive manual log analysis. This helps apply the principle of least-privilege access without blocking or slowing down team productivity.","AWS IAM Access Analyzer, AWS Step Functions, AWS Lambda, AWS CloudTrail, Amazon S3, AWS CodeCommit, Amazon EventBridge",
