111991,0.001653698505833745,0.012023566290736198,-0.0025432133115828037,0.010278617031872272,0.009751691482961178,0.0027982026804238558,-0.0018070751102641225,0.00915430299937725,0.01157204620540142,0.014871087856590748,0.007727017626166344,-0.01354557927697897,0.007099162321537733,-0.026604758575558662,-0.00758702028542757,-0.014143528416752815,0.009505442343652248,-0.0008904178394004703,0.021317830309271812,8.391660230699927e-05,LLM-Powered Policy Change Summarization,"Policy approvers need to efficiently understand complex changes in authorization policies (SCPs/RCPs) within a CI/CD pipeline before approval. Reviewing raw Terraform execution plans and Python logs can be time-consuming and error-prone, making it difficult to grasp the full impact of proposed changes.","A CI/CD pipeline (using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild) for managing AWS Organizations policies (SCPs/RCPs) as infrastructure as code, where policy changes are committed to a remote repository and require a manual approval step before deployment.","Integrate Amazon Bedrock, specifically using the Anthropic Claude Sonnet 3.5 foundation model, into the CI/CD pipeline. A Python script sends a prompt to Amazon Bedrock, providing Terraform execution plans and Python logs (which detail policy merging and optimization) as input. Amazon Bedrock then generates an executive summary of the proposed policy changes. This summary is included in the Amazon SNS notification sent to approvers, enabling them to quickly grasp the impact of the changes before granting approval.","Streamlined policy review process, improved understanding of policy changes for approvers, and reduced the risk of approving unintended policy modifications by providing concise, AI-generated summaries. This helps approvers make informed decisions more efficiently.","Amazon Bedrock (Anthropic Claude Sonnet 3.5), AWS CodePipeline, AWS CodeBuild, Amazon SNS, Terraform, Python scripts",
