26,0.00204229773953557,0.020655037835240364,-0.00615800591185689,0.015974504873156548,0.013425257056951523,-0.0038969446904957294,-0.009107092395424843,0.008526016026735306,0.020109837874770164,0.011007456108927727,-0.00839697103947401,-0.001491435570642352,0.004918047226965427,-0.022313576191663742,-0.002055272227153182,-0.003249732544645667,0.011150053702294827,0.006586186122149229,0.014444003812968731,-0.00979431439191103,AI-Powered Threat Detection (Amazon GuardDuty),"Manually identifying malicious activity and unauthorized behavior in dynamic cloud environments is complex, time-consuming, and prone to missing sophisticated threats. Traditional rule-based systems may struggle with evolving attack patterns and generate excessive false positives.","An AWS environment requiring continuous security monitoring across accounts and regions to protect against various threats, including unusual API calls, suspicious network activity, and compromised instances.","Deploy Amazon GuardDuty, a continuous security monitoring service. GuardDuty automatically analyzes and processes various log sources (e.g., AWS CloudTrail event logs, Amazon VPC Flow Logs, DNS logs) using machine learning, anomaly detection, and integrated threat intelligence feeds. It identifies unexpected, potentially unauthorized, and malicious activity, generating security findings.","Enhanced security posture through automated, continuous threat detection. Early identification of security incidents, reduced manual effort for security analysts, and improved response times to potential compromises.","Amazon GuardDuty, AWS CloudTrail, Amazon VPC Flow Logs, DNS logs",
