09154576109722257,-0.0029997213277965784,0.019967466592788696,-0.004732423461973667,0.011664291843771935,0.00694033969193697,-0.010880548506975174,-0.030132818967103958,0.017508283257484436,0.020269205793738365,0.006566116586327553,-0.005073450971394777,-0.009715007618069649,0.009682570584118366,-0.022795680910348892,0.005497233010828495,-0.010125720873475075,0.0016666599549353123,-0.009633820503950119,0.02592203952372074,-0.010786575265228748,Automated Malware Scanning and File Routing,"Securely transferring files and ensuring all incoming files are scanned for malware before processing, with intelligent routing based on scan results. Traditional methods might involve manual scanning or less integrated solutions, leading to delays or security gaps.",Organizations that need to securely exchange files with external parties via SFTP and validate that all incoming files are free of malware. This is critical for maintaining data integrity and preventing the spread of malicious content within an organization's systems.,"Deploy an SFTP server using AWS Transfer Family with Amazon Cognito authentication. Files uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket are automatically scanned for malware by Amazon GuardDuty's Malware Protection for S3 feature. The scan results (e.g., NOTHREATSFOUND, THREATSFOUND, UNSUPPORTED) trigger an Amazon EventBridge rule. This rule, in turn, invokes a Lambda function that intelligently routes the files to different S3 buckets (e.g., CleanBucket, MalwareBucket, ErrorBucket) based on the scan outcome. If malware is detected, an Amazon SNS topic sends real-time email notifications for security incidents.","Secure file transfer with automated, continuous malware scanning. Files are intelligently routed based on their security status, preventing malicious files from entering clean processing workflows. Real-time alerts enable prompt incident response.","Secure file exchange, supply chain security, data ingestion pipelines, compliance with security standards.",
