16528,-0.010858078487217426,0.017020799219608307,-0.007757547777146101,-0.002625867025926709,0.00018284279212821275,0.0047770291566848755,-0.01798996515572071,0.016333676874637604,-0.0013737673871219158,0.0038197319954633713,-0.008148240856826305,-0.004316508304327726,0.011200004257261753,-0.027041025459766388,-0.019057070836424828,-0.0067087141796946526,0.007562018930912018,0.005984812509268522,0.02404896169900894,-0.009294944815337658,AI-Driven EC2 Compliance Remediation,"Manually managing EC2 instance compliance, ensuring optimal instance type selection, and adhering to best practices (like AWS Well-Architected Framework) is inefficient and slow. There's a need for automated identification and remediation of non-compliant resources.",An organization needs to continuously monitor Amazon EC2 instances for compliance against predefined criteria and automatically remediate non-compliant resources. They want to leverage advanced AI capabilities for intelligent recommendations and automated actions.,"AWS Config rules continuously assess EC2 instances for compliance. Generative AI models in Amazon Bedrock analyze infrastructure patterns to provide intelligent recommendations based on AWS Well-Architected Framework best practices. Amazon Bedrock action groups enable automated remediation steps to address non-compliant instances. The workflow involves user interaction via a Bedrock chat console, triggering action groups and Lambda functions to interact with AWS Config and EC2.","Automated compliance monitoring, AI-driven recommendations for optimal instance type selection and security best practices, automated remediation of non-compliant EC2 instances, scalability, adaptability, and enhanced security posture.","Automated compliance monitoring for EC2 instances, AI-driven recommendations for optimal instance type selection and security best practices, automated remediation of non-compliant EC2 instances, deploying generative AI-based infrastructure.",
