15097094,0.0024564501363784075,0.023488160222768784,-0.0026083930861204863,0.005509441718459129,-0.007635394111275673,-0.002618614584207535,-0.009340210817754269,0.010610062628984451,0.002765475772321224,0.008082961663603783,-0.0022359390277415514,-0.008929812349379063,0.026188109070062637,-0.028444496914744377,-0.009530432522296906,-0.015769120305776596,0.019187964498996735,0.015186664648354053,0.03500346094369888,0.0006536539294756949,Cross-Account SageMaker AI Studio Classic with CodeCommit,"Data scientists or ML engineers in one AWS account need to securely access and work with code repositories (e.g., in CodeCommit) located in a different AWS account, specifically within the Amazon SageMaker AI Studio Classic environment.","An organization uses multiple AWS accounts for different purposes (e.g., development, data, MLOps). Machine Learning development is conducted in Amazon SageMaker AI Studio Classic in one account, while source code is managed in AWS CodeCommit in another account. Secure and efficient cross-account access to the code is required for ML experimentation and development.","The pattern describes associating an AWS CodeCommit repository from one AWS account with Amazon SageMaker AI Studio Classic in another account. This enables seamless access to the code within the ML development environment, likely facilitated by appropriate IAM roles and resource policies.","Enables data scientists and ML engineers to seamlessly access and manage their code from CodeCommit within their SageMaker AI Studio Classic environment, even when resources are in different accounts, promoting collaboration and secure access.","Managing ML project code in a centralized CodeCommit repository while developing in SageMaker AI Studio Classic in a separate account, facilitating secure cross-account collaboration for ML development.",
