05582734942,0.0008625893970020115,0.014361724257469177,-0.00868494063615799,0.00712544983252883,-0.0012860374990850687,-0.007824404165148735,-0.02537616342306137,0.02164834924042225,0.00013853749260306358,0.013551319018006325,-0.000628820329438895,-0.008748405613005161,0.015978258103132248,-0.018107224255800247,-0.01794431544840336,-0.014259038493037224,-0.008205825462937355,-0.00667461846023798,0.029254334047436714,-0.016542986035346985,Multi-Account/Region AI-Driven Operational Insights with DevOps Guru,"In complex, distributed cloud environments spanning multiple AWS accounts and Regions, identifying and diagnosing operational issues (e.g., performance bottlenecks, anomalous behavior) is challenging and time-consuming. Traditional monitoring tools may generate too much noise or require extensive manual configuration.","An organization operates a large-scale AWS environment with applications deployed across multiple accounts and Regions, managed through AWS Organizations. They need an automated, intelligent solution to proactively detect and diagnose operational issues, leveraging machine learning to reduce mean time to resolution (MTTR).","Enable Amazon DevOps Guru across multiple AWS Regions, accounts, and Organizational Units (OUs) using AWS CDK for automated deployment. Amazon DevOps Guru uses machine learning to automatically detect operational anomalies, identify root causes, and recommend remediation actions by analyzing operational data (metrics, logs, events) from various AWS services.","Proactive detection of operational issues, reduced MTTR, automated root cause analysis, intelligent recommendations, and improved overall operational performance and reliability across a large-scale cloud environment.","Proactive anomaly detection in application and infrastructure performance, automated root cause analysis for operational issues, centralized operational insights across a multi-account/multi-region AWS environment.",
