,0.026637738570570946,0.02400374226272106,0.02010129764676094,0.02447507716715336,-0.012508297339081764,0.0005289475084282458,0.0011395503534004092,0.021226759999990463,0.007156378123909235,-0.008197302930057049,-0.016765782609581947,-0.02130342647433281,-0.011765338480472565,-0.033612389117479324,-0.004609228577464819,-0.01307076308876276,0.01240938063710928,0.01021784171462059,0.031127195805311203,-0.012850559316575527,Embedding Text Descriptions of Non-Text Data,"How to incorporate non-textual data (like images, audio, video) into a text-based RAG system when direct multimodal retrieval of the raw media is not required.","Building a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) system where the primary retrieval mechanism is text-based, but the source data includes non-text modalities. The application may not need to display or directly process the raw non-text data in its final output.","Use a text-to-image model or a multimodal Large Language Model (LLM) to generate a textual description of the non-text data. Then, embed this textual representation using standard text embedding models and store it in a vector database. Retrieval is performed using kNN queries on these text embeddings.","Non-textual data can be effectively retrieved using standard text-based similarity searches, providing relevant context to the LLM without the complexity of handling raw media during retrieval or generation. This simplifies the RAG architecture by unifying the embedding space.","Generating text descriptions for real estate listings from property photos; extracting useful text from scanned paper documents using OCR, where the raw image is no longer needed after text extraction.",
