036777325440198183,0.005185436923056841,0.02191590704023838,0.017714770510792732,0.010827920399606228,0.025823116302490234,-0.009943447075784206,0.009062083438038826,0.013659351505339146,0.021429717540740967,0.022644178941845894,0.0021588827949017286,-0.011394405737519264,-0.024710096418857574,-0.014018508605659008,-0.04235154390335083,-0.008101429790258408,-0.013707027770578861,0.009870840236544609,0.012296989560127258,0.031582728028297424,-0.014330035075545311,Multimodal Embeddings with In-Database Media Storage,"How to directly embed and store non-textual data (like images) alongside their vector representations in a unified system, especially when the raw media might be needed for the LLM input or user rendering, and architectural simplicity is prioritized.","Building a multimodal RAG system where direct access to the raw non-text data (e.g., images, diagrams) is important for the application's functionality or for providing richer visual context to a multimodal LLM. The system needs to retrieve both the vector and the associated raw media.","Use a multimodal embedding model (e.g., Amazon Titan) to generate vector representations of non-text data (e.g., JPG or PNG images) in the same semantic vector space as text. Store both the generated embeddings and the raw media (e.g., as BLOBs) directly within the vector database.","Simplifies the data architecture by storing context and raw media in one place, allowing a single query to retrieve both. This can provide the multimodal LLM with additional visual context beyond textual descriptions, potentially leading to more accurate or visually-aware outputs.",AI assistants for field technicians needing to display diagrams from PDF manuals alongside instructions; situations where raw images are needed as direct input to multimodal models to achieve specific visual characteristics or generate images.,
