097044,0.020845459774136543,0.01958511769771576,0.015214484184980392,0.027596447616815567,-0.012470635585486889,0.0038630617782473564,0.001466756104491651,0.018891263753175735,0.005509661044925451,-0.006714193616062403,-0.019477926194667816,-0.022528614848852158,-0.01248062402009964,-0.02732866257429123,-0.002195850946009159,-0.020181605592370033,0.007868978194892406,0.008815517649054527,0.03134061396121979,-0.015667006373405457,Text Embeddings with External Media Pointers,"How to efficiently manage and serve large volumes of non-textual media (e.g., images) in a multimodal RAG system, especially when scalability, performance, or independent media management are critical concerns, making direct in-database storage impractical.","Building a multimodal RAG system where non-text data needs to be retrieved and potentially rendered to the user or provided to an LLM, but the raw media files are large, numerous, or require independent scaling and distribution (e.g., via a Content Delivery Network - CDN).","Host raw non-text media (e.g., images) in external object storage (e.g., cloud storage) or a CDN. Generate text embeddings for textual descriptions of the media (or multimodal embeddings for the media itself, storing only the vector). Store a pointer (e.g., URL) to the external media as metadata alongside the vector embedding in the vector database. When submitting a prompt to the LLM, include the URL of the relevant media.","Provides an inexpensive and scalable way to manage and serve media independently of the vector database. Reduces vector database response size and retrieval latency. Simplifies rendering images in LLM output (e.g., HTML/Markdown with standard image tags) and allows for global distribution of media.",Applications requiring global distribution of media; scenarios where LLMs produce HTML or Markdown output that includes image tags; providing images as input to multimodal models while optimizing storage and retrieval for large datasets.,
