4078179374337196,0.017655516043305397,0.011193417012691498,0.030941328033804893,-0.0061742765828967094,0.002034544013440609,-0.00040963332867249846,0.012474609538912773,0.004461328964680433,-0.007442480884492397,-0.014796300791203976,-0.011680400930345058,-0.009123310446739197,-0.027094058692455292,0.003734018886461854,-0.02033037133514881,0.003059694077819586,0.006293498910963535,0.03506091609597206,-0.012493756599724293,Multimodal Metadata Enrichment for RAG,"How to provide richer, more contextual information to an LLM in a multimodal RAG system beyond just the raw content or its direct textual description, to improve the quality and relevance of LLM outputs.","Building a multimodal RAG system where the LLM's ability to understand, contextualize, and reason about retrieved information can be significantly enhanced by providing structured metadata about the multimodal chunks (e.g., images, text from documents).","Identify and extract relevant metadata from each modality (e.g., file names, timestamps, document titles, jurisdiction, section titles, image captions, page numbers, image format, resolution, document type). Represent this metadata in a structured format (e.g., JSON schema) and store it alongside the content embeddings in the vector database. During retrieval, fetch both the content chunk and its associated metadata, then include this structured metadata in the prompt to the LLM.","LLMs receive more comprehensive and structured context, leading to higher quality, more accurate, and better-reasoned results from the multimodal RAG application. This enables the LLM to better understand the relevance and implications of the retrieved information.","Processing building code documents containing images, where metadata like document title, jurisdiction, section title, and image caption are crucial for the LLM to understand the image's relevance and context; enriching any multimodal RAG system where contextual metadata improves LLM performance.",
