6769447,0.011428297497332096,0.007351059000939131,0.02571580372750759,-0.009217155165970325,-0.0012020330177620053,-0.015549656003713608,0.011202513240277767,0.005651362705975771,-0.004070851020514965,-0.019787589088082314,-0.01887228712439537,-0.0009030858636833727,-0.025056028738617897,-0.01731528900563717,0.012145336717367172,-0.002194406231865287,0.004641781095415354,0.026869196444749832,-0.024022825062274933,AgentG (Agentic Framework for Graph RAG),"Traditional RAG struggles to leverage structured relationships and hierarchies within graph data, limiting multi-hop reasoning and contextual enrichment, especially when combining with unstructured documents.",RAG systems requiring enhanced reasoning and retrieval accuracy by integrating both graph knowledge bases (structured data) and unstructured documents.,"A modular set of agents (Retriever Bank) specializes in retrieving graph-based or unstructured data, dynamically selecting sources. A Critic Module evaluates retrieved data for relevance and quality, triggering feedback loops for refinement. Task-specific agents collaborate to integrate diverse data types, and the LLM synthesizes the validated data.","Enhanced reasoning by combining structured graph relationships with contextual text, dynamic adaptability, improved accuracy through the critic module, and scalable modularity.","Healthcare diagnostics (symptoms, disease relationships), legal research, any application benefiting from combining structured and unstructured knowledge.",
