4989891,0.014874249696731567,0.008663787506520748,0.023805784061551094,-0.009272973984479904,0.006349471863359213,-0.01644814759492874,0.007562502287328243,-0.0020723966881632805,-0.012764100916683674,-0.016661150380969048,-0.025078892707824707,0.004459695424884558,-0.030100151896476746,-0.011189320124685764,-0.0031458691228181124,-0.0070885103195905685,0.012560098432004452,0.031152868643403053,-0.02253846824169159,Graph-Enhanced Agent for Retrieval Augmented Generation (GEAR),"Traditional RAG and LLM agents might struggle to effectively leverage complex, interconnected knowledge that is best represented in a graph structure, limiting their reasoning capabilities over relational data.","LLM applications requiring sophisticated reasoning over highly structured, interconnected knowledge bases, such as knowledge graphs, where relationships between entities are crucial for accurate and deep understanding.","Integrate graph databases or graph neural networks (GNNs) into an Agentic RAG framework. An AI agent can query the graph for relevant entities and relationships, use graph traversal or reasoning to enrich the context, and then feed this graph-derived, structured information to the LLM for more informed generation.","Enhanced reasoning capabilities over structured knowledge, more accurate and contextually rich generations, ability to answer complex questions requiring multi-hop reasoning, and improved knowledge grounding.","Complex question answering, knowledge discovery, semantic search, applications requiring deep understanding of interconnected data, scientific research.",
