29940414,-0.013128301128745079,0.00909388530999422,0.015299179591238499,0.00587585661560297,0.020365821197628975,0.0019493384752422571,0.00694860378280282,-0.013647018000483513,0.016424061730504036,-0.01587621122598648,-0.01519840955734253,-0.013751505874097347,-0.013812210410833359,0.005200830288231373,-0.015686826780438423,-0.012570463120937347,-0.008337825536727905,-0.007171252276748419,0.028803009539842606,0.03976446017622948,-0.017515026032924652,Critic,"Large Language Models (LLMs) might generate incorrect, suboptimal, or unverified outputs, and a mechanism is needed to identify these flaws and guide correction, potentially by interacting with external tools for validation.","Improving the accuracy, reliability, and trustworthiness of LLM outputs, especially in tasks where correctness can be objectively verified, where external tools can provide factual feedback, or where logical consistency is paramount.","An LLM is designated to act as a 'critic,' evaluating the output of another LLM (or its own previous output). This critique process can involve using external tools (e.g., code interpreter, search engine, knowledge base, API calls) to verify facts, check logic, perform calculations, or simulate actions, and then providing structured feedback to guide the generation of a corrected or improved output.","Enhanced self-correction capabilities, improved accuracy and reliability of LLM outputs, effective integration of tools for verification and validation, and reduced hallucination.","Code generation, mathematical problem-solving, fact-checking, complex reasoning tasks where external validation is possible, quality assurance for generated content.",
