005487790331244469,0.018242206424474716,0.018061073496937752,0.017183223739266396,0.03376121446490288,0.0025543649680912495,0.02436138689517975,-0.0026538872625678778,0.003918671049177647,-0.0012094558915123343,0.001199650694616139,-0.018636038526892662,-0.020217182114720345,0.008997068740427494,-0.023509874939918518,-0.009704948402941227,0.009143180213868618,-0.00021338144142646343,0.004653883632272482,0.028023911640048027,-0.021346693858504295,Agent Memory,"Large Language Models (LLMs) have limited context windows, making it challenging for agents to retain and recall information over longer interactions, complex multi-step tasks, or across different sessions, leading to a lack of coherence or inability to learn from past experiences.","Developing LLM-based agents that can engage in long-term conversations, perform multi-step reasoning, adapt their behavior based on historical interactions, or maintain a persistent persona and knowledge base.","Implement a memory system for the agent that stores past interactions, observations, intermediate thoughts, learned knowledge, and relevant context. This memory can be structured (e.g., knowledge graphs, vector databases, episodic buffers) or unstructured (e.g., conversational history) and is selectively retrieved and provided to the LLM as context when needed, often managed by a separate module.","Enhanced long-term coherence in conversations, improved contextual understanding, ability to learn and adapt over time, more sophisticated and personalized agent behavior, and reduced repetition.","Conversational AI, personal assistants, long-running autonomous agents, complex problem-solving, personalized dialogue systems.",
