02156031132,0.01716276817023754,0.0168000441044569,0.024393226951360703,-0.005931167397648096,0.007061162032186985,-0.01246759295463562,0.0051199402660131454,0.000870884454343468,-0.007939357310533524,-0.02212660014629364,-0.013127680867910385,0.006710167974233627,-0.021343668922781944,-0.015384182333946228,0.009133457206189632,0.0012987613445147872,0.010687422007322311,0.03089548833668232,-0.02133692242205143,ReAct (Reasoning and Acting),"Large Language Models (LLMs) struggle to synergistically combine reasoning (e.g., Chain-of-Thought) and acting (e.g., action plan generation) in interactive decision-making, leading to issues like hallucination, error propagation, limited reactive reasoning, and lack of external grounding. Existing acting-only methods lack abstract reasoning or working memory.","Tasks requiring both dynamic, abstract reasoning and interaction with external environments (e.g., knowledge bases, text-based games, web navigation). The agent needs to maintain high-level plans, handle exceptions, and incorporate external information.","Augment the agent's action space to include both domain-specific 'actions' (which affect the external environment and yield observations) and 'thoughts' (language-space actions or reasoning traces that do not affect the environment but update the agent's internal context). These are generated in an interleaved manner, allowing the model to perform dynamic reasoning to create, maintain, and adjust high-level plans for acting ('reason to act') while also interacting with external environments to incorporate additional information into reasoning ('act to reason').","Superior performance over state-of-the-art baselines (Chain-of-Thought, Act-only, imitation/reinforcement learning methods) in few-shot settings. Leads to reduced hallucination, better error handling, improved human interpretability, trustworthiness, and diagnosability across diverse domains.","Multihop Question Answering (HotpotQA), Fact Verification (FEVER), Text-based Games (ALFWorld), Web Navigation (WebShop).",
