5922224223614,0.006969946436583996,0.0032851125579327345,0.004767862614244223,-0.01442715059965849,0.005039113108068705,-0.003760415129363537,0.01512295100837946,0.0024884610902518034,-0.014822699129581451,-0.012101625092327595,-0.010605702176690102,0.00461675925180316,-0.028054313734173775,-0.008735783398151398,0.007162550464272499,-0.003256566822528839,0.02027038484811783,0.03922267258167267,-0.013463122770190239,Self-Consistency for Chain-of-Thought (CoTSC),"Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning, while effective, can be brittle and prone to errors or hallucinations, as it relies on a single reasoning path.","Tasks where Chain-of-Thought prompting is used, and there's a need to improve the robustness and accuracy of the LLM's reasoning process.","During inference, instead of generating a single Chain-of-Thought trajectory, sample multiple diverse CoT trajectories (e.g., by using a decoding temperature > 0). Then, aggregate the results (e.g., by adopting the majority answer among the sampled trajectories) to arrive at a more robust final answer.",Consistently boosts performance over vanilla Chain-of-Thought prompting by leveraging the diversity of multiple reasoning paths. Can be combined with other methods like ReAct for further improvements.,"Question Answering (HotpotQA), Fact Verification (FEVER).",
