734,-0.011351105757057667,0.006492150016129017,0.016977444291114807,0.005212224088609219,0.01604001596570015,-0.007498573511838913,0.001301503973081708,-0.012070778757333755,0.006755187176167965,-0.0033207270316779613,-0.012494332157075405,-0.029405741021037102,-0.014988619834184647,0.0024340185336768627,-0.023706940934062004,-0.01223082933574915,0.011092307977378368,-0.00319245969876647,0.015090536326169968,0.03806547448039055,-0.013767474330961704,Hybrid Reasoning (ReAct + CoTSC),"While ReAct provides factual grounding through external interaction, it can sometimes incur reasoning errors or repetitive loops. Conversely, Chain-of-Thought (CoT) and Self-Consistency (CoTSC) excel at reasoning structure but can hallucinate facts or lack up-to-date knowledge. Neither method is optimal alone for all aspects of knowledge-intensive reasoning.","Knowledge-intensive reasoning tasks where both access to external, up-to-date information and robust internal reasoning capabilities are crucial, and a single approach has limitations.","Combine ReAct and Self-Consistency for Chain-of-Thought (CoTSC) by implementing heuristics to switch between the two methods. For example: If ReAct fails to produce an answer within a set number of steps, back off to CoTSC (leveraging internal reasoning when external interaction is stuck). If CoTSC's majority answer is not confident (e.g., less than half of samples agree), back off to ReAct (seeking external validation when internal knowledge is uncertain).","Achieves the best overall prompting performance on knowledge-intensive tasks by synergistically leveraging the factual grounding of ReAct and the robust reasoning structure of CoTSC, outperforming either method in isolation.","Question Answering (HotpotQA), Fact Verification (FEVER).",
