1571592129766941,0.014296143315732479,0.020518455654382706,0.0038816204760223627,0.02386745810508728,0.0014336012536659837,0.010381078347563744,-0.009342115372419357,0.018669642508029938,-0.0027867730241268873,9.280377707909793e-05,-0.018481247127056122,-0.025376297533512115,0.0020762986969202757,-0.028354478999972343,-0.0016325515462085605,-0.006834306288510561,0.01599358394742012,0.004635253455489874,0.04004449397325516,-0.02210989035665989,Wikipedia API Integration for LLM Grounding,"LLMs, especially in reasoning tasks, suffer from hallucination and outdated knowledge because their internal knowledge is static and not grounded in real-time, verifiable external information.",Knowledge-intensive tasks like question answering and fact verification where access to up-to-date and verifiable external knowledge is critical for accuracy and trustworthiness.,"Design and integrate a simple web API (e.g., Wikipedia API) with specific actions (`search[entity]`, `lookup[string]`, `finish[answer]`) that allow the LLM to interact with an external knowledge source. The LLM uses these actions to retrieve information, simulate browser functionality (Ctrl+F), and provide final answers, thereby grounding its reasoning in external data.",Enables LLMs (especially ReAct) to overcome hallucination and error propagation by retrieving accurate and up-to-date information. Improves factual correctness and trustworthiness of answers.,"HotpotQA, FEVER.",
