86,0.010043461807072163,0.01619533635675907,0.009889592416584492,0.014860996976494789,-0.01791270822286606,0.005233880132436752,-0.009769425727427006,0.008488362655043602,-3.10849973175209e-05,-0.018268084153532982,-0.022332623600959778,-0.006835268810391426,0.01529451459646225,-0.0327344574034214,-0.006330025382339954,0.00012970079842489213,-0.004787613172084093,0.007376189809292555,0.03807654604315758,-0.02325104922056198,Few-Shot Prompting for Agentic LLMs,"Training large language models for complex, interactive tasks often requires vast amounts of labeled data, which is expensive and time-consuming to collect. Traditional fine-tuning can be prohibitive.","When using large, pre-trained language models (LLMs) for new tasks, especially those requiring complex reasoning and action generation (like ReAct), and limited labeled data is available.","Provide the LLM with a small number of 'in-context examples' (few-shot exemplars) within the prompt itself. These examples demonstrate the desired behavior, including interleaved thoughts, actions, and observations (for ReAct), allowing the LLM to generalize to new task instances without extensive fine-tuning.","Enables strong generalization to new task instances with minimal training data (e.g., one to six examples for ReAct), often outperforming methods trained with orders of magnitude more data. Reduces the need for large-scale dataset annotation.","HotpotQA, FEVER, ALFWorld, WebShop.",
