7437,0.009783891029655933,0.007907805033028126,0.0007737020496279001,0.009666787460446358,-0.014071625657379627,0.011128605343401432,-0.008196379989385605,0.006341493688523769,-0.0012148363748565316,-0.00621512345969677,-0.01690666750073433,-0.017496131360530853,0.01179761253297329,-0.02798655815422535,-0.011172350496053696,0.011837217956781387,-0.0036758326459676027,0.006540237460285425,0.03560449555516243,-0.015274859964847565,STaR (Self-Taught Reasoner) / Self-Generated Trajectory Fine-tuning,Manually annotating high-quality reasoning traces and actions at scale for fine-tuning agentic LLMs is challenging and expensive.,"When aiming to improve the performance of agentic LLMs (like ReAct) beyond few-shot prompting, especially for smaller models, but lacking sufficient human-annotated training data.","Employ a bootstrapping approach where the LLM itself (e.g., ReAct) generates a large number of task-solving trajectories (including thoughts, actions, and observations) that lead to correct answers. These self-generated, correct trajectories are then used as training data to fine-tune smaller language models to decode similar trajectories, effectively teaching the model to generate its own rationales.","Enables smaller LLMs to learn complex reasoning and acting behaviors, significantly improving performance over prompting-only methods. Provides a scalable way to generate training data for fine-tuning, making the model learn from its own successful reasoning.",HotpotQA.,
