843422,0.00984877347946167,0.015970144420862198,0.013325920328497887,0.014930766075849533,0.005023057572543621,0.004939594771713018,-0.007755671162158251,0.00041432707803323865,0.0012971238465979695,-0.01487597543746233,-0.023042788729071617,-0.011990923434495926,0.012471302412450314,-0.02162867598235607,-0.004608485382050276,0.02081402763724327,0.010360014624893665,0.011115152388811111,0.02682569809257984,-0.017176726832985878,Act (Pure Acting),"An agent needs to interact with an environment to achieve a goal, but without explicit internal reasoning or planning steps, it can easily get stuck, make suboptimal choices, or fail to recover from errors.","Interactive tasks in environments where direct commands can be issued, but the complexity of the task or the need for error recovery demands more than just sequential action generation. Often used as a baseline to demonstrate the limitations of purely reactive agents.","The LLM directly generates a sequence of actions based on the current observation and the task goal, without explicitly articulating its internal thought process or subgoals. It reacts to the environment by choosing the next action.","Can successfully complete very simple, straightforward tasks. However, it frequently fails on complex, multi-step tasks, gets trapped in repetitive loops, or makes logical errors because it lacks the explicit reasoning to plan, track state, or correct mistakes.","ALFWorld (e.g., 'put a clean knife in countertop'), FEVER (e.g., fact verification), Webshop (e.g., online shopping) as a comparative baseline.",
