9992643595,-0.008163307793438435,0.021120673045516014,0.008777853101491928,0.01929796114563942,0.033365193754434586,0.005086147226393223,0.013192441314458847,-0.006923926994204521,-0.007900348864495754,0.0003773059870582074,-0.017866678535938263,-0.019040901213884354,-0.03006211668252945,0.01896364800632,-0.02094126306474209,-0.003605287754908204,0.01635044440627098,-0.0048534763045609,0.015047166496515274,0.01986043155193329,-0.01757807657122612,Observation-Action Loop,"Agents need to interact dynamically with an environment, adapting their behavior based on real-time feedback, rather than executing a pre-defined, static plan that might not account for environmental changes or unexpected outcomes.","Any interactive environment where an agent's actions change the state of the world, and the agent needs to perceive these changes (observations) to inform subsequent decisions and make progress towards a goal.","The agent continuously cycles through a process of performing an 'Action', receiving an 'Observation' from the environment as a direct result of that action, and then using this observation (potentially after an internal 'Thought' step) to determine the next 'Action'. This creates a continuous feedback loop.","Enables agents to navigate dynamic environments, react to unforeseen circumstances, correct errors, and make progress towards a goal through iterative interaction, leading to more robust and adaptive behavior.","ALFWorld (e.g., 'go to fridge 1' -> 'The fridge 1 is closed' -> 'open fridge 1' -> 'You open the fridge 1...'), FEVER (e.g., 'Action 1 SearchBermuda Triangle' -> 'Observation 1 Reportedly haunted locations'), Webshop (e.g., 'Action search' -> 'Observation Back to Search...').",
